17:22:23 INFO catmaster.llm.factory | [llm.http.raw_post] provider=openrouter model=openai/gpt-5.3-codex:online method=POST url=https://openrouter.ai/api/v1/chat/completions body={"messages":[{"content":"You are an execution controller. Use tool calling to advance the current task.\n\nPriority rules:\n- Use tool calling from all available tools to achieve the goal in the context pack.\n- Check tool names and params carefully.\n- Treat memory index as cross-run historical memory from prior decisions/scientific invariant updates and it may lag current-run progress.\n- For current execution, task packet (goal/detail/expected outputs) is authoritative; use memory for reusable invariants and prior-run context only.\n- Task detail defines the task invariants and done checks. Execute with the minimal non-destructive procedure that satisfies those invariants. Treat task-detail parameters as preferred unless explicitly marked hard, and do bounded self-adjustments before escalating while keeping scientific/computational invariants fixed.\n- Tool schemas are authoritative for argument shapes/defaults; do not re-invent parameter templates in bash scripts.\n- Do not initiate file edits on your own. Only edit files when the current task packet explicitly requires editing/writing outputs for this task. For `MEMORY/**`, only update when scientific invariants, method definitions, or final reusable results changed.\n- If file editing is explicitly required by the task packet, prefer `apply_aider_edits` for deterministic edits (including memory files) over ad-hoc in-place shell edits.\n\nExecution rules:\n- Do not rerun the same preparation tool with identical parameters if the previous call already succeeded and required artifacts still exist. Prefer reusing and validating existing outputs.\n- Do not trigger expensive reruns purely for path/layout normalization when numerical/physical requirements are already satisfied.\n- Bundle independent filesystem operations in the same turn whenever possible, but do not issue concurrent write calls; keep write/edit/move/create operations sequential and verify each write step before the next.\n- For simple multi-directory setup or one-shot workspace reconnaissance, prefer a single focused bash_exec over many single-path filesystem tool calls.\n- Perform only checks required to satisfy current done criteria; avoid speculative or perfection-oriented extra validation.\n- For routine checks, keep bash output small: prefer focused queries (`rg -n`, `head`, `tail`) and avoid broad/full-file dumps unless deep debugging is required.\n- Prefer read_multiple_files when you need several small text files at once.\n- Progressive disclosure is mandatory: memory_index_excerpt is short; discover paths with `search_files` / `list_directory` / `directory_tree`, then read small windows via `read_text_file(head=..., tail=...)`.\n- Use `bash_exec` for shell execution, content grep (`rg`), parser invocation, and external binaries.\n- Internal metadata audit logs are not task inputs; do not read or reference them in task reasoning.\n- By default, do not generate long markdown reports via `cat <<'MD'`.\n\nParsing policy:\n- Debug triage should prioritize focused, minimal evidence extraction and concise failure signatures.\n- For extracting final numerical results across many calculations (for comparison/reporting), avoid repeated manual grep stitching; prefer parser libraries or small single-purpose scripts.\n- Prefer mature third-party libraries for parsing and post-analysis when available; avoid reimplementing standard parsers/analysis logic from scratch.\n- Common Python packages are available and preferred when relevant: ase, pymatgen, numpy, matplotlib, scipy, pandas, fitz, requests.\n- For actual workload execution (batch processing, long runs, or outputs to be reused/audited), write reusable script files and keep each script focused/small.\n\nTermination and handoff:\n- End with one concise final handoff that clearly states the task status and reusable outputs.\n- Use `status=\"done\"` when task is complete.\n- Use `status=\"blocked\"` only when still blocked after bounded self-adjustment attempts on non-critical execution parameters, or when hard scientific invariants conflict.\n- Follow schema field descriptions for per-field content quality and placeholders; do not fill fields with invented content.\n- For remote/batch job failures, do one minimal triage (failing status file, stdout/stderr snippets, key inputs) and attempt one focused fix.\n- Do not do open-ended exploration for remote failures (no SSH). If failure persists, return `status=\"blocked\"` with failed paths, evidence pointers, likely cause, and a minimal rerun/repair plan that reruns only the failed subset.\n- Keep handoff evidence-based and concise; avoid redundant repetition across fields.\n- Function tools must be invoked via tool calls. Do NOT put function tool names into bash_exec commands.\n- Keep stdout concise; if persistent command logs are needed, use pipeline logging to project files (e.g., `cmd 2>&1 | tee reports/<task_desc>/run.log`) and print short summaries.\n- Always provide file or directory paths as relative paths; they will be resolved relative to the project files root.\n","role":"system"},{"content":"<context_pack>\nTask goal:\nRun a VASP relaxation for gas-phase O2 in a large cubic box and extract final energy/atom and O–O bond length.\n\nTask detail:\n1) Create a new workdir `o2_vasp/relax/`.\n2) Build O2 geometry (SMILES `O=O`) and place in a cubic cell with ~15–20 Å vacuum (e.g., 18 Å) centered; write a structure file usable by VASP prep (POSCAR or an intermediate format your prep tool accepts).\n3) Prepare VASP relaxation inputs from scratch in that folder (INCAR/KPOINTS/POSCAR/POTCAR) using PBE PAW for O. Use Gamma-only KPOINTS 1x1x1. Use spin-polarization for triplet O2 (ISPIN=2; initialize MAGMOM ~1 1 and/or set NUPDOWN=2). Recommend: PREC=Accurate, ENCUT=520 (or >= POTCAR ENMAX), EDIFF=1e-6, EDIFFG=-0.02, ISMEAR=0 SIGMA=0.05, IBRION=2, NSW=100, ISIF=2, ISYM=0, LCHARG=.FALSE., LWAVE=.FALSE.\n4) Execute VASP in that directory (single job) until convergence. Ensure outputs include OUTCAR, OSZICAR, CONTCAR.\n5) Parse results: (a) final TOTEN from OUTCAR (last ionic step) and compute energy per atom = TOTEN/2 in eV/atom; (b) compute O–O distance from CONTCAR final positions (Å).\n6) Write a short `o2_vasp/RESULTS.md` summarizing: settings used, final energy (eV), energy/atom (eV/atom), bond length (Å), and point to evidence lines/paths (e.g., OUTCAR grep output, CONTCAR).\n\nExpected outputs:\n- Directory `o2_vasp/relax/` containing INCAR, KPOINTS, POSCAR, POTCAR, and VASP outputs (OUTCAR, OSZICAR, CONTCAR).\n- `o2_vasp/RESULTS.md` with final TOTEN (eV), energy per atom (eV/atom), and O–O bond length (Å) plus file/line references or extracted snippets.\n\nSuggested tools:\ncreate_molecule_from_smiles, vasp_relax_prepare, vasp_execute_batch, bash_exec, read_text_file, write_file\n\nReference hint:\n- If `vasp_relax_prepare` needs a structure file, generate an XYZ first then convert/write POSCAR.\n- Use `grep -n \"free  energy   TOTEN\" OUTCAR | tail -1` to capture final TOTEN line.\n- Bond length: parse CONTCAR (Cartesian) and compute distance between the two atoms via a tiny python snippet in bash.\n\nWorkspace policy:\nProject files policy:\n- Treat \".\" as the project files root.\n- All path parameters and returned paths are relative to \".\".\n- Never use absolute paths or metadata paths.\n- Use search_files / list_directory / directory_tree to discover files.\n- Use read_text_file with head/tail for progressive disclosure.\n- Use bash_exec for shell commands, content grep, parser invocation, and external binaries.\n- Role: task_runner\n\nMemory index excerpt:\n# MEMORY (AUTOLOADED INDEX)\n\n## What this is\n- Autoloaded memory index for this project.\n- Keep this file concise and pointer-first.\n- Put details in MEMORY/topics/*.md.\n\n## Latest State\n- Current focus: Compute O2 in a box: prepare VASP inputs from scratch, DO perform VASP calculation to get the results, and report final energy per atom and O–O bond distance from vasp results.\n- Current milestone: (empty)\n- Latest run artifact: (empty)\n- Next action: (empty)\n\n## Top Constraints\n1. (empty)\n\n## Active Open Questions\n1. (empty)\n\n## Pointers\n- Facts / decisions: MEMORY/topics/FACTS.md\n- Files / artifacts: MEMORY/topics/FILES.md\n- Constraints: MEMORY/topics/CONSTRAINTS.md\n- Open questions: MEMORY/topics/QUESTIONS.md\n- Runbook: MEMORY/topics/RUNBOOK.md\n\n## Keyword Map\n- GOAL: objective, success criteria, scope, non-goals\n- FACTS: definition, verified, result, decision\n- FILES: path, artifact, dataset, output, script\n- CONSTRAINTS: must, cannot, policy, budget\n- QUESTIONS: unknown, blocked, clarify, decide\n- RUNBOOK: steps, checklist, verify\n\n</context_pack>\n","role":"user"},{"content":null,"role":"assistant","tool_calls":[{"type":"function","id":"call_NLAqyx4HYI4uImLrpUJQ3jgo","function":{"name":"bash_exec","arguments":"{\"script\": \"set -e\\nmkdir -p o2_vasp/relax\\nprintf 'created o2_vasp/relax\\\\n'\\nls -la o2_vasp\", \"cwd\": \".\", \"timeout_s\": 120, \"no_network\": true}"}}]},{"content":"stdout:\ncreated o2_vasp/relax\ntotal 12\ndrwxr-xr-x 3 root root 4096 Mar  3 17:21 .\ndrwxr-xr-x 4 root root 4096 Mar  3 17:21 ..\ndrwxr-xr-x 2 root root 4096 Mar  3 17:21 relax\n\nexit_code=0 timed_out=False cancelled=False cwd=. timeout_s=120.0\nOffload: _tool_outputs/bash_exec/bash_exec_20260303T092152947189Z_bf00889a.json","role":"tool","tool_call_id":"call_NLAqyx4HYI4uImLrpUJQ3jgo"},{"content":null,"role":"assistant","tool_calls":[{"type":"function","id":"call_4wr72H1u1SwOyVJwdFqACxhS","function":{"name":"create_molecule_from_smiles","arguments":"{\"smiles\": \"O=O\", \"name\": \"O2\", \"output_path\": \"o2_vasp/relax/o2\", \"box_padding\": 9, \"fmt\": \"both\"}"}}]},{"content":"create_molecule_from_smiles completed.\nformula=O2 natoms=2\nxyz_file_rel=o2_vasp/relax/o2.xyz poscar_file_rel=o2_vasp/relax/o2.vasp","role":"tool","tool_call_id":"call_4wr72H1u1SwOyVJwdFqACxhS"},{"content":null,"role":"assistant","tool_calls":[{"type":"function","id":"call_5jHw8cDeUnGwFibV0EEcXEEN","function":{"name":"vasp_relax_prepare","arguments":"{\"input_path\": \"o2_vasp/relax/o2.vasp\", \"output_root\": \"o2_vasp/relax\", \"calc_type\": \"gas\", \"relax_cell\": false, \"k_product\": 30, \"use_d3\": false, \"use_dft_plus_u\": false, \"compute_dos\": false, \"enable_dipole\": false}"}}]},{"content":"vasp_relax_prepare completed.\nstructures_processed=1 errors_count=0 calc_type=gas\noutput_root_rel=o2_vasp/relax\nfirst_prepared_dir=o2_vasp/relax/o2","role":"tool","tool_call_id":"call_5jHw8cDeUnGwFibV0EEcXEEN"}],"model":"openai/gpt-5.3-codex:online","reasoning_effort":"medium","stream":false,"temperature":1.0,"tool_choice":"required","tools":[{"type":"function","function":{"name":"create_molecule_from_smiles","description":"Build a 3D molecule from a SMILES string using RDKit. Specially, pay attention to the formal charge of the SMILES string, RDkit will check the charge and add Hs to the molecule to make it neutral.","parameters":{"properties":{"smiles":{"description":"SMILES string for the molecule.","type":"string"},"name":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string"},{"type":"null"}],"default":null,"description":"Optional base name for output files; defaults to formula."},"output_path":{"default":"mol","description":"Workspace-relative path prefix; files will be <prefix>.xyz and/or <prefix>.vasp.","type":"string"},"box_padding":{"default":10.0,"description":"Padding (Å) added around the molecule to make a cubic box for POSCAR. Box lattice is around twice the padding value (10A Padding -> 20A Box).","minimum":0.0,"type":"number"},"fmt":{"default":"poscar","description":"Output format: poscar (with PBC box), xyz (no PBC), or both.","pattern":"^(poscar|xyz|both)$","type":"string"}},"required":["smiles"],"type":"object","additionalProperties":false}}},{"type":"function","function":{"name":"mace_relax_batch","description":"Submit multiple MACE relaxations in one DPDispatcher submission. Preferred tool for batch MACE relaxations.","parameters":{"properties":{"input_dir":{"description":"Root directory containing structure files with lattice (POSCAR/CIF).","type":"string"},"output_root":{"description":"Root directory to store batch outputs. Results mirror the input directory structure; each input file expands to a folder without suffix (e.g. input_dir/a/c.vasp -> output_root/a/c/opt.vasp). Must be outside input_dir.","type":"string"},"fmax":{"default":0.02,"description":"Force threshold for relaxation in eV/Angstrom.","exclusiveMinimum":0,"type":"number"},"maxsteps":{"default":500,"description":"Max steps for relaxation.","minimum":1,"type":"integer"},"model":{"default":"mh-1","description":"MACE model name. Recommended options: 'mh-1' (slower, higher accuracy) or 'medium-mpa-0' (faster, lower accuracy).","examples":["mh-1","medium-mpa-0"],"type":"string"},"head":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string"},{"type":"null"}],"default":"omat_pbe","description":"Model head for multi-head models (e.g. 'omat_pbe'). Use empty string to disable."},"dispersion":{"default":false,"description":"Enable dispersion correction in mace_mp. Default: false.","type":"boolean"},"relax_lattice":{"default":false,"description":"Whether to relax lattice/cell together with atomic positions via ASE FrechetCellFilter.","type":"boolean"},"check_interval":{"default":30,"description":"Polling interval in seconds when waiting.","type":"integer"}},"required":["input_dir","output_root"],"type":"object","additionalProperties":false}}},{"type":"function","function":{"name":"mace_sp_batch","description":"Run MACE single-point jobs for structures under one directory.","parameters":{"properties":{"input_dir":{"description":"Input directory containing structures (POSCAR/CONTCAR/CIF/VASP).","type":"string"},"output_root":{"description":"Output root for batch results. Must be outside input_dir.","type":"string"},"model":{"default":"mh-1","description":"MACE model name (e.g., mh-1, medium-mpa-0).","examples":["mh-1","medium-mpa-0"],"type":"string"},"head":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string"},{"type":"null"}],"default":"omat_pbe","description":"Model head for multi-head models. Use empty string to disable."},"dispersion":{"default":false,"description":"Enable dispersion correction.","type":"boolean"},"check_interval":{"default":30,"description":"Polling interval in seconds when waiting.","type":"integer"}},"required":["input_dir","output_root"],"type":"object","additionalProperties":false}}},{"type":"function","function":{"name":"vasp_relax_prepare","description":"Prepare MPRelaxSet-based VASP relax inputs with calc_type presets and k_product k-mesh.\n    Also can be modified for other calculation types by overriding INCAR via the user_incar_settings.\n    Support exts: .vasp, .cif\n\n    Baseline DFT settings follow Materials Project MPRelaxSet (key defaults):\n    - PBE54 POTCARS, ENCUT=520 eV, PREC=Accurate, ISPIN=2, IBRION=2, LREAL=AUTO, LASPH=True, LWAVE=False, LCHARG=False.\n    - Additional overrides applied based on calc_type: ISMEAR=0, SIGMA=0.1 for bulk/slab; ISMEAR=0, SIGMA=0.01 for gas.\n    - ISIF policy: bulk with relax_cell=False -> ISIF=2; bulk with relax_cell=True -> ISIF=3.\n      slab and gas always use ISIF=2, where slab forces KPOINTS z=1 and gas forces KPOINTS 1x1x1 with ISYM=0, LREAL=False.\n    - Improved convergence settings: EDIFF=1e-6; NSW=500; EDIFFG=-0.02;\n    - LORBIT is controlled by compute_dos (default False -> LORBIT=0, True -> LORBIT=11).\n    - KPOINTS is generated by k*a=k_product, where a is the lattice constant in Angstrom. Set to 30 by default and sufficient for most systems.\n    - DFT-D3 and DFT+U are disabled by default. Enable them if the system is adsorption system(DFT-D3) or transition metal oxide system(DFT+U).","parameters":{"properties":{"input_path":{"description":"Path to a structure file with lattice information (POSCAR/CIF) or a directory containing multiple structures. Support exts: .vasp, .cif","type":"string"},"output_root":{"description":"Root directory for generated VASP inputs (one subfolder per input structure). If input_path is a file: output_root/<stem>/...; if input_path is a directory, preserve relative subfolders: output_root/<relpath>/<stem>/...","type":"string"},"calc_type":{"default":"bulk","description":"Calculation type: 'gas'|'bulk'|'slab'. This provides preset INCAR overrides for different calculation types. gas is suitable for small molecules; slab is suitable for surface slab models; bulk is suitable for bulk relaxations.","enum":["gas","bulk","slab"],"type":"string"},"relax_cell":{"default":false,"description":"Whether to relax cell shape/volume (ISIF=3). Only valid when calc_type='bulk'.","type":"boolean"},"k_product":{"default":30,"description":"Target k-mesh density via k_i~round(k_product/L_i), min 1, forced odd (Gamma-centered); gas always 1x1x1.","minimum":1,"type":"integer"},"use_d3":{"default":false,"description":"Enable DFT-D3 Correction (IVDW=11). Enable it for adsorption calculations.","type":"boolean"},"use_dft_plus_u":{"default":false,"description":"Enable DFT+U relevant settings according to materials project standard. Enable it for Transition Metal Oxide systems.","type":"boolean"},"compute_dos":{"default":false,"description":"Enable DOS/projection output by setting LORBIT=11. Default false (LORBIT=0) to reduce disk usage.","type":"boolean"},"enable_dipole":{"default":false,"description":"Enable dipole correction helper. When true, default IDIPOL=3 and set DIPOL to the atomic center of mass of cell in fractional coordinates.","type":"boolean"},"user_incar_settings":{"additionalProperties":true,"description":"User INCAR overrides as a json object as per pymatgen's user_incar_settings format, e.g. {\"MAGMOM\":{\"O\":1},\"ALGO\":\"Fast\"}. In this tool, due to pymatgen constraints, MAGMOM/LDAUU/LDAUJ must be provided as symbol:value maps. Use null only as a value inside the override object to remove a specific INCAR key, e.g. `{\"LREAL\": null}`. calc_type/task-required presets still take precedence on key conflict.","type":"object"}},"required":["input_path","output_root"],"type":"object","additionalProperties":false}}},{"type":"function","function":{"name":"vasp_sp_prepare","description":"Prepare MPRelaxSet-based VASP single-point inputs for structures under a file or directory. Parameters are the same as VaspRelaxPrepareInput, but with single_point relaxation enabled (NSW=0, IBRION=-1).","parameters":{"properties":{"input_path":{"description":"Structure file or directory of structures. Supported: .vasp, .cif","type":"string"},"output_root":{"description":"Root directory for generated VASP inputs (one subfolder per structure).","type":"string"},"calc_type":{"default":"bulk","description":"Calculation preset for k-mesh and INCAR defaults.","enum":["gas","bulk","slab"],"type":"string"},"k_product":{"default":30,"description":"k-mesh density via k_i~round(k_product/L_i), min 1.","minimum":1,"type":"integer"},"use_d3":{"default":false,"description":"Enable DFT-D3 correction (IVDW=11).","type":"boolean"},"use_dft_plus_u":{"default":false,"description":"Enable DFT+U settings.","type":"boolean"},"compute_dos":{"default":false,"description":"Enable DOS/projection output by setting LORBIT=11. Default false (LORBIT=0).","type":"boolean"},"enable_dipole":{"default":false,"description":"Enable dipole correction helper. When true, default IDIPOL=3 and set DIPOL to the atomic center of mass in fractional coordinates.","type":"boolean"},"user_incar_settings":{"additionalProperties":true,"description":"User INCAR overrides as a json object as per pymatgen's user_incar_settings format, e.g. {\"MAGMOM\":{\"O\":1},\"ALGO\":\"Fast\"}. In this tool, due to pymatgen constraints, MAGMOM/LDAUU/LDAUJ must be provided as symbol:value maps. Use null only as a value inside the override object to remove a specific INCAR key, e.g. `{\"LORBIT\": null}`. calc_type/task-required presets still take precedence on key conflict.","type":"object"}},"required":["input_path","output_root"],"type":"object","additionalProperties":false}}},{"type":"function","function":{"name":"build_slab","description":"Build slabs for all terminations of a Miller index from bulk structure(s).\n\n    Provide exactly one of bulk_structure or bulk_dir. When bulk_dir is used, output_root is required.\n    Batch outputs are written under output_root/<slab_id>/..., where slab_id encodes the relative input path\n    (without suffix) using '__'.","parameters":{"properties":{"bulk_structure":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string"},{"type":"null"}],"default":null,"description":"Bulk structure file (POSCAR/CIF/etc.), workspace-relative."},"bulk_dir":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string"},{"type":"null"}],"default":null,"description":"Directory containing bulk structure files for batch slab building."},"miller_index":{"description":"Miller index [h,k,l].","items":{"type":"integer"},"maxItems":3,"minItems":3,"type":"array"},"output_root":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string"},{"type":"null"}],"default":null,"description":"Directory to write the slab structures. Required for bulk_dir; defaults to 'slabs' for single file. For bulk_dir, outputs are written under output_root/<slab_id>/..., where slab_id encodes the relative input path (without suffix) using '__'."},"slab_thickness":{"default":12.0,"description":"Target slab thickness (Å).","minimum":0.0,"type":"number"},"vacuum_thickness":{"default":15.0,"description":"Vacuum thickness (Å).","minimum":0.0,"type":"number"},"supercell":{"default":[1,1,1],"description":"Supercell replication [a,b,c] for slab structure after generation.","items":{"type":"integer"},"maxItems":3,"minItems":3,"type":"array"},"get_symmetry_slab":{"default":false,"description":"If true, returned slabs will ensure top and bottom surfaces are identical. Use it for surface energy calculation.","type":"boolean"},"orthogonal":{"default":false,"description":"If true, convert each slab to an orthogonal c-oriented cell. Useful for grain boundary generation.","type":"boolean"},"lll_reduce":{"default":false,"description":"Apply LLL reduction during slab generation. Not recommended to use unless necessary.","type":"boolean"}},"required":["miller_index"],"type":"object","additionalProperties":false}}},{"type":"function","function":{"name":"fix_atoms_by_layers","description":"Fix (freeze) the bottom N atomic layers of slab structure(s).\n\n    Provide exactly one of structure_ref or structure_dir. When structure_dir is used, output_dir is required.\n    Batch outputs are written to output_dir/<slab_id>.vasp and a summary JSON is written to\n    output_dir/batch_fix_atoms_by_layers.json.","parameters":{"properties":{"structure_ref":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string"},{"type":"null"}],"default":null,"description":"Slab structure file to modify (POSCAR/CIF)."},"structure_dir":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string"},{"type":"null"}],"default":null,"description":"Directory containing slab structure files to modify."},"output_path":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string"},{"type":"null"}],"default":null,"description":"Output structure path (workspace-relative) for single file."},"output_dir":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string"},{"type":"null"}],"default":null,"description":"Output directory for batch mode. Outputs are written as <output_dir>/<slab_id>.vasp where slab_id encodes the relative input path (without suffix) using '__'."},"freeze_layers":{"description":"Number of bottom layers to freeze. Use layer_tol to group layers.","minimum":0,"type":"integer"},"centralize":{"default":false,"description":"Recentre slab along c before applying constraints.","type":"boolean"},"layer_tol":{"default":0.2,"description":"Layer grouping tolerance in Å. 0.2 is suitable for most cases except for highly tilted slabs.","exclusiveMinimum":0.0,"type":"number"}},"required":["freeze_layers"],"type":"object","additionalProperties":false}}},{"type":"function","function":{"name":"fix_atoms_by_height","description":"Fix (freeze) atoms within specified z ranges of slab structure(s).\n\n    Provide exactly one of structure_ref or structure_dir. When structure_dir is used, output_dir is required.\n    Batch outputs are written to output_dir/<slab_id>.vasp and a summary JSON is written to\n    output_dir/batch_fix_atoms_by_height.json.","parameters":{"properties":{"structure_ref":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string"},{"type":"null"}],"default":null,"description":"Slab structure file to modify (POSCAR/CIF)."},"structure_dir":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string"},{"type":"null"}],"default":null,"description":"Directory containing slab structure files to modify."},"output_path":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string"},{"type":"null"}],"default":null,"description":"Output structure path (workspace-relative) for single file."},"output_dir":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string"},{"type":"null"}],"default":null,"description":"Output directory for batch mode. Outputs are written as <output_dir>/<slab_id>.vasp where slab_id encodes the relative input path (without suffix) using '__'."},"z_ranges":{"description":"Ranges in Å in Cartesian coordinates; atoms in these z ranges are frozen.","items":{"properties":{"z_min":{"description":"Lower bound (Å) in Cartesian coordinates.","type":"number"},"z_max":{"description":"Upper bound (Å) in Cartesian coordinates.","type":"number"}},"required":["z_min","z_max"],"type":"object","additionalProperties":false},"minItems":1,"type":"array"},"centralize":{"default":false,"description":"Recentre slab along c after applying constraints.","type":"boolean"}},"required":["z_ranges"],"type":"object","additionalProperties":false}}},{"type":"function","function":{"name":"supercell","description":"Create supercells from structure file(s). THIS WILL LOSE ALL SELECTIVE DYNAMICS INFORMATION.\n    Provide exactly one of structure_file or structure_dir. When structure_dir is used, output_dir is required.\n    Batch outputs are written to output_dir/<structure_id>.vasp and a summary JSON is written to\n    output_dir/batch_supercell.json.\n\n    The JSON format is:\n    {\n      \"results\": [\n        {\"input_rel\": \"a/CO.vasp\", \"structure_id\": \"a__CO\", \"output_rel\": \"out/a__CO.vasp\", \"natoms\": 2}\n      ]\n    }","parameters":{"properties":{"structure_file":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string"},{"type":"null"}],"default":null,"description":"Bulk structure file (POSCAR/CIF/etc.), workspace-relative."},"structure_dir":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string"},{"type":"null"}],"default":null,"description":"Directory containing structure files for batch supercell generation."},"supercell":{"description":"Supercell replication [a,b,c].","items":{"type":"integer"},"maxItems":3,"minItems":3,"type":"array"},"output_path":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string"},{"type":"null"}],"default":null,"description":"Output structure path for single structure (workspace-relative, e.g., bulk_supercell.vasp)."},"output_dir":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string"},{"type":"null"}],"default":null,"description":"Output directory for batch mode. Outputs are written as <output_dir>/<structure_id>.vasp where structure_id encodes the relative input path (without suffix) using '__'."}},"required":["supercell"],"type":"object","additionalProperties":false}}},{"type":"function","function":{"name":"enumerate_adsorption_sites","description":"Enumerate adsorption sites on a slab using ASF. Use it only for small scale placement.\n\n    The tool writes a JSON list to output_json:\n    [\n      {\"label\": \"ontop_0\", \"kind\": \"ontop\", \"cart_coords\": [x, y, z]}\n    ]\n    The returned tool data includes the workspace-relative path in \"sites\" and \"sites_json_rel\".","parameters":{"properties":{"slab_file":{"description":"Slab structure file (POSCAR/CONTCAR/CIF), workspace-relative.","type":"string"},"mode":{"default":"all","description":"Which site families to return: all|ontop|bridge|hollow.","type":"string"},"distance":{"default":2.0,"description":"Height above surface to sample adsorption sites (Å).","minimum":0.0,"type":"number"},"output_json":{"default":"adsorption/sites.json","description":"Output JSON path for site list (workspace-relative).","type":"string"}},"required":["slab_file"],"type":"object","additionalProperties":false}}},{"type":"function","function":{"name":"place_adsorbate","description":"Place an adsorbate molecule on a slab. Use it only if for small scale placement.\n    This tool keeps selective dynamics of the original slab structure and allows adsorbate to move freely.\n    It writes metadata sidecar <output>.meta.json and an ads_indices index JSON.","parameters":{"properties":{"slab_file":{"description":"Slab structure file (POSCAR/CONTCAR/CIF).","type":"string"},"adsorbate_file":{"description":"Adsorbate molecule file (XYZ).","type":"string"},"site":{"default":"auto","description":"Site label like ontop_0|bridge_1|hollow_2 or 'auto' (which use all[0]).","type":"string"},"distance":{"default":2.0,"description":"Height used to generate adsorption sites (Å).","minimum":0.0,"type":"number"},"output_poscar":{"default":"adsorption/adsorbed.vasp","description":"Output POSCAR path (workspace-relative).","type":"string"}},"required":["slab_file","adsorbate_file"],"type":"object","additionalProperties":false}}},{"type":"function","function":{"name":"generate_batch_adsorption_structures","description":"Generate multiple adsorbed structures up to max_structures. Suitable for large scale placement.\n    This tool keeps selective dynamics of the original slab structure and allows adsorbate to move freely.\n    Input can be a single slab file (slab_file) or a directory of slab files (slab_dir).\n    When slab_dir is used, each slab gets its own subdirectory under output_dir. Max_structures applies per slab.\n    For nested slab_dir layouts, slab_id encodes the relative path (without suffix) using '__'.\n\n    The tool writes a JSON list to output_dir/batch_structures.json and a per-structure\n    metadata sidecar <output>.meta.json with ads_indices.\n    It also writes output_dir/ads_indices.json as an index file:\n    [\n      {\n        \"slab_file_rel\": \"slabs/fe111.vasp\",\n        \"slab_id\": \"fe111\",\n        \"label\": \"ontop_0\",\n        \"output_poscar_rel\": \"adsorption/batch/fe111/ontop_0.vasp\",\n        \"ads_indices_added\": [36],\n        \"ads_indices\": [36]\n      }\n    ]\n    The returned tool data replaces \"structures\" with the workspace-relative path to this JSON file.","parameters":{"properties":{"slab_file":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string"},{"type":"null"}],"default":null,"description":"Slab structure file (POSCAR/CONTCAR/CIF)."},"slab_dir":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string"},{"type":"null"}],"default":null,"description":"Directory containing slab files for high-throughput placement."},"adsorbate_file":{"description":"Adsorbate molecule file (XYZ).","type":"string"},"mode":{"default":"all","description":"all|ontop|bridge|hollow","type":"string"},"distance":{"default":2.0,"description":"Height used to generate adsorption sites (Å).","minimum":0.0,"type":"number"},"max_structures":{"default":1000,"description":"Maximum number of adsorbed structures to generate.","minimum":1,"type":"integer"},"output_dir":{"default":"adsorption/batch","description":"Directory to write batch POSCARs.","type":"string"}},"required":["adsorbate_file"],"type":"object","additionalProperties":false}}},{"type":"function","function":{"name":"make_neb_geometry","description":"Generate NEB interpolation geometries in nebmake.pl style.\n\n    The tool validates that initial and final structures have the same element order, atom count,\n    and lattice (within tolerance). Images are written under output_dir/00..(NI+1) with output_filename.\n    Selective dynamics constraints are preserved if present in the input files (ASE handles constraints).","parameters":{"properties":{"initial_path":{"description":"Initial structure file (POSCAR/CONTCAR/.vasp/.cif).","type":"string"},"final_path":{"description":"Final structure file (POSCAR/CONTCAR/.vasp/.cif).","type":"string"},"n_images":{"description":"Number of intermediate images (NI).","minimum":1,"type":"integer"},"output_dir":{"default":"neb_images","description":"Output directory for image folders (workspace-relative).","type":"string"},"output_filename":{"default":"POSCAR","description":"Filename for each image output (e.g., POSCAR).","type":"string"},"interp_mode":{"default":"direct","description":"Output coordinate style when writing POSCAR: direct (fractional) or cartesian.","pattern":"^(direct|cartesian)$","type":"string"},"interp_method":{"default":"linear","description":"Interpolation method: linear or idpp.","pattern":"^(linear|idpp)$","type":"string"},"vtst_wrap":{"default":true,"description":"If true, wrap fractional coordinates into [0,1) before interpolation (VTST nebmake.pl behavior).","type":"boolean"},"overwrite":{"default":false,"description":"If true, overwrite output_dir if it exists.","type":"boolean"}},"required":["initial_path","final_path","n_images"],"type":"object","additionalProperties":false}}},{"type":"function","function":{"name":"make_neb_incar","description":"Generate a VTST NEB/CI-NEB INCAR based on a template INCAR.\n\n    The tool parses the template INCAR (ignores comments/blank lines, case-insensitive keys),\n    applies NEB overrides, and writes the final INCAR along with a patch JSON.","parameters":{"properties":{"template_incar_path":{"description":"Template INCAR path (workspace-relative).","type":"string"},"output_incar_path":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string"},{"type":"null"}],"default":null,"description":"Output INCAR path. If omitted, uses output_dir/INCAR."},"output_dir":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string"},{"type":"null"}],"default":"neb_inputs","description":"Output directory for INCAR and patch JSON (workspace-relative)."},"images":{"description":"Number of intermediate images (IMAGES).","minimum":1,"type":"integer"},"climb":{"default":false,"description":"Enable CI-NEB with LCLIMB=.TRUE. if true.","type":"boolean"},"iopt":{"default":7,"description":"IOPT value for VTST optimizer (allowed: 7/2/1).","type":"integer"},"ediff":{"anyOf":[{"type":"number"},{"type":"null"}],"default":null,"description":"Override EDIFF if provided."},"ediffg":{"anyOf":[{"type":"number"},{"type":"null"}],"default":null,"description":"Override EDIFFG if provided."},"spring":{"anyOf":[{"type":"number"},{"type":"null"}],"default":null,"description":"Override SPRING if provided."},"potim":{"anyOf":[{"type":"number"},{"type":"null"}],"default":0.0,"description":"Override POTIM (default 0)."},"additional_overrides":{"additionalProperties":true,"description":"Additional INCAR overrides as a dict; highest priority and can override required defaults. In this tool, due to pymatgen constraints, MAGMOM/LDAUU/LDAUJ must be provided as symbol:value maps. If not provided, no user override is applied and this tool's default INCAR strategy is used. Use null value to remove a key from INCAR.","type":"object"}},"required":["template_incar_path","images"],"type":"object","additionalProperties":false}}},{"type":"function","function":{"name":"vasp_execute_batch","description":"Submit VASP runs in one DPDispatcher submission (single-folder or recursive batch modes).","parameters":{"properties":{"input_dir":{"description":"Input directory for VASP execution. Two modes are supported: (1) single-folder mode: input_dir itself is a VASP calc folder containing INCAR and POTCAR; (2) batch mode: recursively discover subfolders containing INCAR and POTCAR. Nested mode is forbidden when input_dir itself is a calc folder and descendants also contain calc folders.","type":"string"},"output_dir":{"description":"Root directory to store outputs. In single-folder mode, results go to output_dir/<basename(input_dir)>. In batch mode, results mirror discovered subfolder layout under output_dir. Must not be inside input_dir. Staging directories under output_dir are cleaned after completion.","type":"string"},"check_interval":{"default":30,"description":"Polling interval seconds","type":"integer"}},"required":["input_dir","output_dir"],"type":"object","additionalProperties":false}}},{"type":"function","function":{"name":"mp_search_materials","description":"Search Materials Project with flexible criteria and write results to CSV.\n\n    Common criteria keys (pass via `criteria`):\n      - material_ids (list[str] or str)\n      - elements (list[str] or str)\n      - chemsys (str)\n      - formula (str)\n      - is_stable (bool)\n      - energy_above_hull ([min, max])\n      - formation_energy ([min, max])\n      - band_gap ([min, max])\n      - crystal_system (str)\n      - spacegroup_number / spacegroup_symbol\n      - num_sites ([min, max])\n      - density ([min, max])\n      - volume ([min, max])\n      - num_elements ([min, max])\n    Common fields for output rows (pass via `fields`):\n      material_id, formula_pretty (or formula), energy_above_hull, formation_energy_per_atom (or formation_energy),\n      band_gap, crystal_system, spacegroup_number, spacegroup_symbol, nsites (or num_sites), density, volume.","parameters":{"properties":{"criteria":{"additionalProperties":true,"description":"Direct summary.search filters as a dict (keys listed above). Range values may be [min, max].","type":"object"},"fields":{"description":"Fields to include in CSV rows; supports common aliases.","items":{"type":"string"},"type":"array"},"limit":{"default":50,"description":"Maximum number of hits to return (default 50).","minimum":1,"type":"integer"},"output_csv":{"description":"Workspace-relative CSV path to write search results.","type":"string"}},"required":["output_csv"],"type":"object","additionalProperties":false}}},{"type":"function","function":{"name":"mp_download_structure","description":"Download one or more structures from Materials Project into the workspace.","parameters":{"properties":{"mp_ids":{"description":"Materials Project IDs, e.g., ['mp-149', 'mp-13'].","items":{"type":"string"},"type":"array"},"fmt":{"default":"poscar","description":"Output format: poscar|cif|json.","pattern":"^(poscar|cif|json)$","type":"string"},"output_dir":{"default":"retrieval/mp","description":"Workspace-relative directory to save the structure.","type":"string"}},"required":["mp_ids"],"type":"object","additionalProperties":false}}},{"type":"function","function":{"name":"bash_exec","description":"Execute a multi-line bash script inside the workspace (default) and return stdout/stderr.\n    Network access is disabled by default using Linux network namespaces (unshare).\n    Symbolic link operations are disabled; use copy/move operations instead.\n    Stdout/stderr are returned as-is and projection/offload is handled centrally.\n    Keep output short in scripts and print one-line summaries when possible.","parameters":{"properties":{"script":{"description":"Bash script to execute (multi-line).","type":"string"},"cwd":{"default":".","description":"Working directory inside project files root.","type":"string"},"timeout_s":{"default":86400.0,"description":"Timeout seconds.","minimum":0.1,"type":"number"},"no_network":{"default":true,"description":"Disable network using unshare network namespace.","type":"boolean"}},"required":["script"],"type":"object","additionalProperties":false}}},{"type":"function","function":{"name":"apply_aider_edits","description":"Apply Aider SEARCH/REPLACE edit blocks to workspace files.","parameters":{"properties":{"edits_text":{"description":"Aider SEARCH/REPLACE edit blocks text. Format per block:\n<relative/path/to/file>\n<<<<<<< SEARCH\n... exact existing text ...\n=======\n... replacement text ...\n>>>>>>> REPLACE","type":"string"},"allowed_paths":{"description":"Optional project-files-relative path prefixes. Use [] to allow edits anywhere under workspace root.","items":{"type":"string"},"type":"array"},"emit_diff":{"default":true,"description":"Whether to return unified diff text for audit.","type":"boolean"}},"required":["edits_text"],"type":"object","additionalProperties":false}}},{"type":"function","function":{"name":"read_text_file","description":"Read the complete contents of a file from the file system as text. Handles various text encodings and provides detailed error messages if the file cannot be read. Use this tool when you need to examine the contents of a single file. Use the 'head' parameter to read only the first N lines of a file, or the 'tail' parameter to read only the last N lines of a file. Operates on the file as text regardless of extension. Only works within allowed directories.","parameters":{"$schema":"http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#","type":"object","properties":{"path":{"type":"string"},"tail":{"description":"If provided, returns only the last N lines of the file","type":"number"},"head":{"description":"If provided, returns only the first N lines of the file","type":"number"}},"required":["path"]}}},{"type":"function","function":{"name":"read_multiple_files","description":"Read the contents of multiple files simultaneously. This is more efficient than reading files one by one when you need to analyze or compare multiple files. Each file's content is returned with its path as a reference. Failed reads for individual files won't stop the entire operation. Only works within allowed directories.","parameters":{"$schema":"http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#","type":"object","properties":{"paths":{"minItems":1,"type":"array","items":{"type":"string"},"description":"Array of file paths to read. Each path must be a string pointing to a valid file within allowed directories."}},"required":["paths"]}}},{"type":"function","function":{"name":"write_file","description":"Create a new file or completely overwrite an existing file with new content. Use with caution as it will overwrite existing files without warning. Handles text content with proper encoding. Only works within allowed directories.","parameters":{"$schema":"http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#","type":"object","properties":{"path":{"type":"string"},"content":{"type":"string"}},"required":["path","content"]}}},{"type":"function","function":{"name":"edit_file","description":"Make line-based edits to a text file. Each edit replaces exact line sequences with new content. Returns a git-style diff showing the changes made. Only works within allowed directories.","parameters":{"$schema":"http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#","type":"object","properties":{"path":{"type":"string"},"edits":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"object","properties":{"oldText":{"type":"string","description":"Text to search for - must match exactly"},"newText":{"type":"string","description":"Text to replace with"}},"required":["oldText","newText"]}},"dryRun":{"default":false,"description":"Preview changes using git-style diff format","type":"boolean"}},"required":["path","edits"]}}},{"type":"function","function":{"name":"create_directory","description":"Create a new directory or ensure a directory exists. Can create multiple nested directories in one operation. If the directory already exists, this operation will succeed silently. Perfect for setting up directory structures for projects or ensuring required paths exist. Only works within allowed directories.","parameters":{"$schema":"http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#","type":"object","properties":{"path":{"type":"string"}},"required":["path"]}}},{"type":"function","function":{"name":"list_directory","description":"Get a detailed listing of all files and directories in a specified path. Results clearly distinguish between files and directories with [FILE] and [DIR] prefixes. This tool is essential for understanding directory structure and finding specific files within a directory. Only works within allowed directories.","parameters":{"$schema":"http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#","type":"object","properties":{"path":{"type":"string"}},"required":["path"]}}},{"type":"function","function":{"name":"directory_tree","description":"Get a recursive tree view of files and directories as a JSON structure. Each entry includes 'name', 'type' (file/directory), and 'children' for directories. Files have no children array, while directories always have a children array (which may be empty). The output is formatted with 2-space indentation for readability. Only works within allowed directories.","parameters":{"$schema":"http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#","type":"object","properties":{"path":{"type":"string"},"excludePatterns":{"default":[],"type":"array","items":{"type":"string"}}},"required":["path"]}}},{"type":"function","function":{"name":"move_file","description":"Move or rename files and directories. Can move files between directories and rename them in a single operation. If the destination exists, the operation will fail. Works across different directories and can be used for simple renaming within the same directory. Both source and destination must be within allowed directories.","parameters":{"$schema":"http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#","type":"object","properties":{"source":{"type":"string"},"destination":{"type":"string"}},"required":["source","destination"]}}},{"type":"function","function":{"name":"search_files","description":"Recursively search for files and directories matching a pattern. The patterns should be glob-style patterns that match paths relative to the working directory. Use pattern like '*.ext' to match files in current directory, and '**/*.ext' to match files in all subdirectories. Returns full paths to all matching items. Great for finding files when you don't know their exact location. Only searches within allowed directories.","parameters":{"$schema":"http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#","type":"object","properties":{"path":{"type":"string"},"pattern":{"type":"string"},"excludePatterns":{"default":[],"type":"array","items":{"type":"string"}}},"required":["path","pattern"]}}},{"type":"function","function":{"name":"TaskOutput","description":"Structured output from the task runner agent.","parameters":{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"status":{"description":"Task terminal status. Use 'done' only when task acceptance criteria are satisfied; use 'blocked' when progress is blocked by unresolved issues.","enum":["done","blocked"],"type":"string"},"summary":{"description":"Concise task outcome/failure summary with key file pointers. Do not paste long tables/logs/scripts; cite file paths instead.","type":"string"},"facts":{"description":"Only high-value verified facts reusable downstream (include units/conditions/evidence path when relevant). Do not restate command traces. Use [] when none.","items":{"type":"string"},"type":"array"},"files":{"description":"Only key reproducibility/user-facing artifact paths (files or directories). Use a directory path when it is a clearer bundle-level reference. Avoid listing low-value scratch files. Use [] when none.","items":{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"path":{"description":"Workspace-relative artifact path (file or directory). Always use project-relative paths; do not use absolute paths.","type":"string"},"description":{"description":"Short one-line description.","type":"string"},"kind":{"description":"Artifact category. Common values: script, output, report, log. Use 'dir' when the path points to a directory bundle.","type":"string"}},"required":["path","description","kind"],"type":"object"},"type":"array"},"constraints":{"description":"Only new/changed constraints. Use [] when none.","items":{"type":"string"},"type":"array"},"open_questions":{"description":"Only unresolved blockers affecting next steps. Do not include speculative questions. Use [] when none.","items":{"type":"string"},"type":"array"},"decisions":{"description":"Only decisions materially affecting downstream work; avoid duplicating summary/facts content. Use [] when none.","items":{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"decision":{"description":"Short decision statement.","type":"string"},"rationale":{"description":"Brief rationale (one short sentence preferred).","type":"string"}},"required":["decision","rationale"],"type":"object"},"type":"array"},"next_steps":{"description":"Only immediate actionable next steps. Use [] when no next step is required.","items":{"type":"string"},"type":"array"},"artifacts":{"description":"Supporting artifact paths when needed. Use [] when none.","items":{"type":"string"},"type":"array"},"error":{"description":"Failure reason for status=blocked. For status=done, use empty string ''.","type":"string"},"needs_human":{"description":"Whether a human must intervene for status=blocked. For status=done, set false.","type":"boolean"},"hint":{"description":"Optional concise recovery hint for status=blocked. For status=done, use empty string ''.","type":"string"}},"required":["status","summary","facts","files","constraints","open_questions","decisions","next_steps","artifacts","error","needs_human","hint"],"type":"object"}}}],"prompt_cache_retention":"24h"}
17:22:23 INFO httpx | HTTP Request: POST https://openrouter.ai/api/v1/chat/completions "HTTP/1.1 200 OK"
17:22:30 INFO catmaster.llm.factory | [llm.http.raw_post] provider=openrouter model=openai/gpt-5.3-codex:online method=POST url=https://openrouter.ai/api/v1/chat/completions body={"messages":[{"content":"You are an execution controller. Use tool calling to advance the current task.\n\nPriority rules:\n- Use tool calling from all available tools to achieve the goal in the context pack.\n- Check tool names and params carefully.\n- Treat memory index as cross-run historical memory from prior decisions/scientific invariant updates and it may lag current-run progress.\n- For current execution, task packet (goal/detail/expected outputs) is authoritative; use memory for reusable invariants and prior-run context only.\n- Task detail defines the task invariants and done checks. Execute with the minimal non-destructive procedure that satisfies those invariants. Treat task-detail parameters as preferred unless explicitly marked hard, and do bounded self-adjustments before escalating while keeping scientific/computational invariants fixed.\n- Tool schemas are authoritative for argument shapes/defaults; do not re-invent parameter templates in bash scripts.\n- Do not initiate file edits on your own. Only edit files when the current task packet explicitly requires editing/writing outputs for this task. For `MEMORY/**`, only update when scientific invariants, method definitions, or final reusable results changed.\n- If file editing is explicitly required by the task packet, prefer `apply_aider_edits` for deterministic edits (including memory files) over ad-hoc in-place shell edits.\n\nExecution rules:\n- Do not rerun the same preparation tool with identical parameters if the previous call already succeeded and required artifacts still exist. Prefer reusing and validating existing outputs.\n- Do not trigger expensive reruns purely for path/layout normalization when numerical/physical requirements are already satisfied.\n- Bundle independent filesystem operations in the same turn whenever possible, but do not issue concurrent write calls; keep write/edit/move/create operations sequential and verify each write step before the next.\n- For simple multi-directory setup or one-shot workspace reconnaissance, prefer a single focused bash_exec over many single-path filesystem tool calls.\n- Perform only checks required to satisfy current done criteria; avoid speculative or perfection-oriented extra validation.\n- For routine checks, keep bash output small: prefer focused queries (`rg -n`, `head`, `tail`) and avoid broad/full-file dumps unless deep debugging is required.\n- Prefer read_multiple_files when you need several small text files at once.\n- Progressive disclosure is mandatory: memory_index_excerpt is short; discover paths with `search_files` / `list_directory` / `directory_tree`, then read small windows via `read_text_file(head=..., tail=...)`.\n- Use `bash_exec` for shell execution, content grep (`rg`), parser invocation, and external binaries.\n- Internal metadata audit logs are not task inputs; do not read or reference them in task reasoning.\n- By default, do not generate long markdown reports via `cat <<'MD'`.\n\nParsing policy:\n- Debug triage should prioritize focused, minimal evidence extraction and concise failure signatures.\n- For extracting final numerical results across many calculations (for comparison/reporting), avoid repeated manual grep stitching; prefer parser libraries or small single-purpose scripts.\n- Prefer mature third-party libraries for parsing and post-analysis when available; avoid reimplementing standard parsers/analysis logic from scratch.\n- Common Python packages are available and preferred when relevant: ase, pymatgen, numpy, matplotlib, scipy, pandas, fitz, requests.\n- For actual workload execution (batch processing, long runs, or outputs to be reused/audited), write reusable script files and keep each script focused/small.\n\nTermination and handoff:\n- End with one concise final handoff that clearly states the task status and reusable outputs.\n- Use `status=\"done\"` when task is complete.\n- Use `status=\"blocked\"` only when still blocked after bounded self-adjustment attempts on non-critical execution parameters, or when hard scientific invariants conflict.\n- Follow schema field descriptions for per-field content quality and placeholders; do not fill fields with invented content.\n- For remote/batch job failures, do one minimal triage (failing status file, stdout/stderr snippets, key inputs) and attempt one focused fix.\n- Do not do open-ended exploration for remote failures (no SSH). If failure persists, return `status=\"blocked\"` with failed paths, evidence pointers, likely cause, and a minimal rerun/repair plan that reruns only the failed subset.\n- Keep handoff evidence-based and concise; avoid redundant repetition across fields.\n- Function tools must be invoked via tool calls. Do NOT put function tool names into bash_exec commands.\n- Keep stdout concise; if persistent command logs are needed, use pipeline logging to project files (e.g., `cmd 2>&1 | tee reports/<task_desc>/run.log`) and print short summaries.\n- Always provide file or directory paths as relative paths; they will be resolved relative to the project files root.\n","role":"system"},{"content":"<context_pack>\nTask goal:\nRun a VASP relaxation for gas-phase O2 in a large cubic box and extract final energy/atom and O–O bond length.\n\nTask detail:\n1) Create a new workdir `o2_vasp/relax/`.\n2) Build O2 geometry (SMILES `O=O`) and place in a cubic cell with ~15–20 Å vacuum (e.g., 18 Å) centered; write a structure file usable by VASP prep (POSCAR or an intermediate format your prep tool accepts).\n3) Prepare VASP relaxation inputs from scratch in that folder (INCAR/KPOINTS/POSCAR/POTCAR) using PBE PAW for O. Use Gamma-only KPOINTS 1x1x1. Use spin-polarization for triplet O2 (ISPIN=2; initialize MAGMOM ~1 1 and/or set NUPDOWN=2). Recommend: PREC=Accurate, ENCUT=520 (or >= POTCAR ENMAX), EDIFF=1e-6, EDIFFG=-0.02, ISMEAR=0 SIGMA=0.05, IBRION=2, NSW=100, ISIF=2, ISYM=0, LCHARG=.FALSE., LWAVE=.FALSE.\n4) Execute VASP in that directory (single job) until convergence. Ensure outputs include OUTCAR, OSZICAR, CONTCAR.\n5) Parse results: (a) final TOTEN from OUTCAR (last ionic step) and compute energy per atom = TOTEN/2 in eV/atom; (b) compute O–O distance from CONTCAR final positions (Å).\n6) Write a short `o2_vasp/RESULTS.md` summarizing: settings used, final energy (eV), energy/atom (eV/atom), bond length (Å), and point to evidence lines/paths (e.g., OUTCAR grep output, CONTCAR).\n\nExpected outputs:\n- Directory `o2_vasp/relax/` containing INCAR, KPOINTS, POSCAR, POTCAR, and VASP outputs (OUTCAR, OSZICAR, CONTCAR).\n- `o2_vasp/RESULTS.md` with final TOTEN (eV), energy per atom (eV/atom), and O–O bond length (Å) plus file/line references or extracted snippets.\n\nSuggested tools:\ncreate_molecule_from_smiles, vasp_relax_prepare, vasp_execute_batch, bash_exec, read_text_file, write_file\n\nReference hint:\n- If `vasp_relax_prepare` needs a structure file, generate an XYZ first then convert/write POSCAR.\n- Use `grep -n \"free  energy   TOTEN\" OUTCAR | tail -1` to capture final TOTEN line.\n- Bond length: parse CONTCAR (Cartesian) and compute distance between the two atoms via a tiny python snippet in bash.\n\nWorkspace policy:\nProject files policy:\n- Treat \".\" as the project files root.\n- All path parameters and returned paths are relative to \".\".\n- Never use absolute paths or metadata paths.\n- Use search_files / list_directory / directory_tree to discover files.\n- Use read_text_file with head/tail for progressive disclosure.\n- Use bash_exec for shell commands, content grep, parser invocation, and external binaries.\n- Role: task_runner\n\nMemory index excerpt:\n# MEMORY (AUTOLOADED INDEX)\n\n## What this is\n- Autoloaded memory index for this project.\n- Keep this file concise and pointer-first.\n- Put details in MEMORY/topics/*.md.\n\n## Latest State\n- Current focus: Compute O2 in a box: prepare VASP inputs from scratch, DO perform VASP calculation to get the results, and report final energy per atom and O–O bond distance from vasp results.\n- Current milestone: (empty)\n- Latest run artifact: (empty)\n- Next action: (empty)\n\n## Top Constraints\n1. (empty)\n\n## Active Open Questions\n1. (empty)\n\n## Pointers\n- Facts / decisions: MEMORY/topics/FACTS.md\n- Files / artifacts: MEMORY/topics/FILES.md\n- Constraints: MEMORY/topics/CONSTRAINTS.md\n- Open questions: MEMORY/topics/QUESTIONS.md\n- Runbook: MEMORY/topics/RUNBOOK.md\n\n## Keyword Map\n- GOAL: objective, success criteria, scope, non-goals\n- FACTS: definition, verified, result, decision\n- FILES: path, artifact, dataset, output, script\n- CONSTRAINTS: must, cannot, policy, budget\n- QUESTIONS: unknown, blocked, clarify, decide\n- RUNBOOK: steps, checklist, verify\n\n</context_pack>\n","role":"user"},{"content":null,"role":"assistant","tool_calls":[{"type":"function","id":"call_NLAqyx4HYI4uImLrpUJQ3jgo","function":{"name":"bash_exec","arguments":"{\"script\": \"set -e\\nmkdir -p o2_vasp/relax\\nprintf 'created o2_vasp/relax\\\\n'\\nls -la o2_vasp\", \"cwd\": \".\", \"timeout_s\": 120, \"no_network\": true}"}}]},{"content":"stdout:\ncreated o2_vasp/relax\ntotal 12\ndrwxr-xr-x 3 root root 4096 Mar  3 17:21 .\ndrwxr-xr-x 4 root root 4096 Mar  3 17:21 ..\ndrwxr-xr-x 2 root root 4096 Mar  3 17:21 relax\n\nexit_code=0 timed_out=False cancelled=False cwd=. timeout_s=120.0\nOffload: _tool_outputs/bash_exec/bash_exec_20260303T092152947189Z_bf00889a.json","role":"tool","tool_call_id":"call_NLAqyx4HYI4uImLrpUJQ3jgo"},{"content":null,"role":"assistant","tool_calls":[{"type":"function","id":"call_4wr72H1u1SwOyVJwdFqACxhS","function":{"name":"create_molecule_from_smiles","arguments":"{\"smiles\": \"O=O\", \"name\": \"O2\", \"output_path\": \"o2_vasp/relax/o2\", \"box_padding\": 9, \"fmt\": \"both\"}"}}]},{"content":"create_molecule_from_smiles completed.\nformula=O2 natoms=2\nxyz_file_rel=o2_vasp/relax/o2.xyz poscar_file_rel=o2_vasp/relax/o2.vasp","role":"tool","tool_call_id":"call_4wr72H1u1SwOyVJwdFqACxhS"},{"content":null,"role":"assistant","tool_calls":[{"type":"function","id":"call_5jHw8cDeUnGwFibV0EEcXEEN","function":{"name":"vasp_relax_prepare","arguments":"{\"input_path\": \"o2_vasp/relax/o2.vasp\", \"output_root\": \"o2_vasp/relax\", \"calc_type\": \"gas\", \"relax_cell\": false, \"k_product\": 30, \"use_d3\": false, \"use_dft_plus_u\": false, \"compute_dos\": false, \"enable_dipole\": false}"}}]},{"content":"vasp_relax_prepare completed.\nstructures_processed=1 errors_count=0 calc_type=gas\noutput_root_rel=o2_vasp/relax\nfirst_prepared_dir=o2_vasp/relax/o2","role":"tool","tool_call_id":"call_5jHw8cDeUnGwFibV0EEcXEEN"},{"content":null,"role":"assistant","tool_calls":[{"type":"function","id":"call_lHpu2I0UUEw3BsBalLeYGNYu","function":{"name":"bash_exec","arguments":"{\"script\": \"set -e\\nfind o2_vasp -maxdepth 3 -type f | sort\\nprintf '\\\\nINCAR:\\\\n'\\ncat o2_vasp/relax/o2/INCAR\\nprintf '\\\\nKPOINTS:\\\\n'\\ncat o2_vasp/relax/o2/KPOINTS\", \"cwd\": \".\", \"timeout_s\": 120, \"no_network\": true}"}}]},{"content":"stdout:\no2_vasp/relax/o2.vasp\no2_vasp/relax/o2.xyz\no2_vasp/relax/o2/INCAR\no2_vasp/relax/o2/KPOINTS\no2_vasp/relax/o2/POSCAR\no2_vasp/relax/o2/POTCAR\n\nINCAR:\nALGO = Fast\nEDIFF = 1e-06\nEDIFFG = -0.02\nENCUT = 520.0\nIBRION = 2\nISIF = 2\nISMEAR = 0\nISPIN = 2\nISYM = 0\nLASPH = True\nLCHARG = False\nLDAU = False\nLORBIT = 0\nLREAL = False\nLWAVE = False\nMAGMOM = 2*0.6\nNELM = 100\nNSW = 500\nPREC = Accurate\nSIGMA = 0.01\n\nKPOINTS:\nAutomatic kpoint scheme\n0\nGamma\n1 1 1\n\nexit_code=0 timed_out=False cancelled=False cwd=. timeout_s=120.0\nOffload: _tool_outputs/bash_exec/bash_exec_20260303T092230287978Z_9794df37.json","role":"tool","tool_call_id":"call_lHpu2I0UUEw3BsBalLeYGNYu"}],"model":"openai/gpt-5.3-codex:online","reasoning_effort":"medium","stream":false,"temperature":1.0,"tool_choice":"required","tools":[{"type":"function","function":{"name":"create_molecule_from_smiles","description":"Build a 3D molecule from a SMILES string using RDKit. Specially, pay attention to the formal charge of the SMILES string, RDkit will check the charge and add Hs to the molecule to make it neutral.","parameters":{"properties":{"smiles":{"description":"SMILES string for the molecule.","type":"string"},"name":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string"},{"type":"null"}],"default":null,"description":"Optional base name for output files; defaults to formula."},"output_path":{"default":"mol","description":"Workspace-relative path prefix; files will be <prefix>.xyz and/or <prefix>.vasp.","type":"string"},"box_padding":{"default":10.0,"description":"Padding (Å) added around the molecule to make a cubic box for POSCAR. Box lattice is around twice the padding value (10A Padding -> 20A Box).","minimum":0.0,"type":"number"},"fmt":{"default":"poscar","description":"Output format: poscar (with PBC box), xyz (no PBC), or both.","pattern":"^(poscar|xyz|both)$","type":"string"}},"required":["smiles"],"type":"object","additionalProperties":false}}},{"type":"function","function":{"name":"mace_relax_batch","description":"Submit multiple MACE relaxations in one DPDispatcher submission. Preferred tool for batch MACE relaxations.","parameters":{"properties":{"input_dir":{"description":"Root directory containing structure files with lattice (POSCAR/CIF).","type":"string"},"output_root":{"description":"Root directory to store batch outputs. Results mirror the input directory structure; each input file expands to a folder without suffix (e.g. input_dir/a/c.vasp -> output_root/a/c/opt.vasp). Must be outside input_dir.","type":"string"},"fmax":{"default":0.02,"description":"Force threshold for relaxation in eV/Angstrom.","exclusiveMinimum":0,"type":"number"},"maxsteps":{"default":500,"description":"Max steps for relaxation.","minimum":1,"type":"integer"},"model":{"default":"mh-1","description":"MACE model name. Recommended options: 'mh-1' (slower, higher accuracy) or 'medium-mpa-0' (faster, lower accuracy).","examples":["mh-1","medium-mpa-0"],"type":"string"},"head":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string"},{"type":"null"}],"default":"omat_pbe","description":"Model head for multi-head models (e.g. 'omat_pbe'). Use empty string to disable."},"dispersion":{"default":false,"description":"Enable dispersion correction in mace_mp. Default: false.","type":"boolean"},"relax_lattice":{"default":false,"description":"Whether to relax lattice/cell together with atomic positions via ASE FrechetCellFilter.","type":"boolean"},"check_interval":{"default":30,"description":"Polling interval in seconds when waiting.","type":"integer"}},"required":["input_dir","output_root"],"type":"object","additionalProperties":false}}},{"type":"function","function":{"name":"mace_sp_batch","description":"Run MACE single-point jobs for structures under one directory.","parameters":{"properties":{"input_dir":{"description":"Input directory containing structures (POSCAR/CONTCAR/CIF/VASP).","type":"string"},"output_root":{"description":"Output root for batch results. Must be outside input_dir.","type":"string"},"model":{"default":"mh-1","description":"MACE model name (e.g., mh-1, medium-mpa-0).","examples":["mh-1","medium-mpa-0"],"type":"string"},"head":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string"},{"type":"null"}],"default":"omat_pbe","description":"Model head for multi-head models. Use empty string to disable."},"dispersion":{"default":false,"description":"Enable dispersion correction.","type":"boolean"},"check_interval":{"default":30,"description":"Polling interval in seconds when waiting.","type":"integer"}},"required":["input_dir","output_root"],"type":"object","additionalProperties":false}}},{"type":"function","function":{"name":"vasp_relax_prepare","description":"Prepare MPRelaxSet-based VASP relax inputs with calc_type presets and k_product k-mesh.\n    Also can be modified for other calculation types by overriding INCAR via the user_incar_settings.\n    Support exts: .vasp, .cif\n\n    Baseline DFT settings follow Materials Project MPRelaxSet (key defaults):\n    - PBE54 POTCARS, ENCUT=520 eV, PREC=Accurate, ISPIN=2, IBRION=2, LREAL=AUTO, LASPH=True, LWAVE=False, LCHARG=False.\n    - Additional overrides applied based on calc_type: ISMEAR=0, SIGMA=0.1 for bulk/slab; ISMEAR=0, SIGMA=0.01 for gas.\n    - ISIF policy: bulk with relax_cell=False -> ISIF=2; bulk with relax_cell=True -> ISIF=3.\n      slab and gas always use ISIF=2, where slab forces KPOINTS z=1 and gas forces KPOINTS 1x1x1 with ISYM=0, LREAL=False.\n    - Improved convergence settings: EDIFF=1e-6; NSW=500; EDIFFG=-0.02;\n    - LORBIT is controlled by compute_dos (default False -> LORBIT=0, True -> LORBIT=11).\n    - KPOINTS is generated by k*a=k_product, where a is the lattice constant in Angstrom. Set to 30 by default and sufficient for most systems.\n    - DFT-D3 and DFT+U are disabled by default. Enable them if the system is adsorption system(DFT-D3) or transition metal oxide system(DFT+U).","parameters":{"properties":{"input_path":{"description":"Path to a structure file with lattice information (POSCAR/CIF) or a directory containing multiple structures. Support exts: .vasp, .cif","type":"string"},"output_root":{"description":"Root directory for generated VASP inputs (one subfolder per input structure). If input_path is a file: output_root/<stem>/...; if input_path is a directory, preserve relative subfolders: output_root/<relpath>/<stem>/...","type":"string"},"calc_type":{"default":"bulk","description":"Calculation type: 'gas'|'bulk'|'slab'. This provides preset INCAR overrides for different calculation types. gas is suitable for small molecules; slab is suitable for surface slab models; bulk is suitable for bulk relaxations.","enum":["gas","bulk","slab"],"type":"string"},"relax_cell":{"default":false,"description":"Whether to relax cell shape/volume (ISIF=3). Only valid when calc_type='bulk'.","type":"boolean"},"k_product":{"default":30,"description":"Target k-mesh density via k_i~round(k_product/L_i), min 1, forced odd (Gamma-centered); gas always 1x1x1.","minimum":1,"type":"integer"},"use_d3":{"default":false,"description":"Enable DFT-D3 Correction (IVDW=11). Enable it for adsorption calculations.","type":"boolean"},"use_dft_plus_u":{"default":false,"description":"Enable DFT+U relevant settings according to materials project standard. Enable it for Transition Metal Oxide systems.","type":"boolean"},"compute_dos":{"default":false,"description":"Enable DOS/projection output by setting LORBIT=11. Default false (LORBIT=0) to reduce disk usage.","type":"boolean"},"enable_dipole":{"default":false,"description":"Enable dipole correction helper. When true, default IDIPOL=3 and set DIPOL to the atomic center of mass of cell in fractional coordinates.","type":"boolean"},"user_incar_settings":{"additionalProperties":true,"description":"User INCAR overrides as a json object as per pymatgen's user_incar_settings format, e.g. {\"MAGMOM\":{\"O\":1},\"ALGO\":\"Fast\"}. In this tool, due to pymatgen constraints, MAGMOM/LDAUU/LDAUJ must be provided as symbol:value maps. Use null only as a value inside the override object to remove a specific INCAR key, e.g. `{\"LREAL\": null}`. calc_type/task-required presets still take precedence on key conflict.","type":"object"}},"required":["input_path","output_root"],"type":"object","additionalProperties":false}}},{"type":"function","function":{"name":"vasp_sp_prepare","description":"Prepare MPRelaxSet-based VASP single-point inputs for structures under a file or directory. Parameters are the same as VaspRelaxPrepareInput, but with single_point relaxation enabled (NSW=0, IBRION=-1).","parameters":{"properties":{"input_path":{"description":"Structure file or directory of structures. Supported: .vasp, .cif","type":"string"},"output_root":{"description":"Root directory for generated VASP inputs (one subfolder per structure).","type":"string"},"calc_type":{"default":"bulk","description":"Calculation preset for k-mesh and INCAR defaults.","enum":["gas","bulk","slab"],"type":"string"},"k_product":{"default":30,"description":"k-mesh density via k_i~round(k_product/L_i), min 1.","minimum":1,"type":"integer"},"use_d3":{"default":false,"description":"Enable DFT-D3 correction (IVDW=11).","type":"boolean"},"use_dft_plus_u":{"default":false,"description":"Enable DFT+U settings.","type":"boolean"},"compute_dos":{"default":false,"description":"Enable DOS/projection output by setting LORBIT=11. Default false (LORBIT=0).","type":"boolean"},"enable_dipole":{"default":false,"description":"Enable dipole correction helper. When true, default IDIPOL=3 and set DIPOL to the atomic center of mass in fractional coordinates.","type":"boolean"},"user_incar_settings":{"additionalProperties":true,"description":"User INCAR overrides as a json object as per pymatgen's user_incar_settings format, e.g. {\"MAGMOM\":{\"O\":1},\"ALGO\":\"Fast\"}. In this tool, due to pymatgen constraints, MAGMOM/LDAUU/LDAUJ must be provided as symbol:value maps. Use null only as a value inside the override object to remove a specific INCAR key, e.g. `{\"LORBIT\": null}`. calc_type/task-required presets still take precedence on key conflict.","type":"object"}},"required":["input_path","output_root"],"type":"object","additionalProperties":false}}},{"type":"function","function":{"name":"build_slab","description":"Build slabs for all terminations of a Miller index from bulk structure(s).\n\n    Provide exactly one of bulk_structure or bulk_dir. When bulk_dir is used, output_root is required.\n    Batch outputs are written under output_root/<slab_id>/..., where slab_id encodes the relative input path\n    (without suffix) using '__'.","parameters":{"properties":{"bulk_structure":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string"},{"type":"null"}],"default":null,"description":"Bulk structure file (POSCAR/CIF/etc.), workspace-relative."},"bulk_dir":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string"},{"type":"null"}],"default":null,"description":"Directory containing bulk structure files for batch slab building."},"miller_index":{"description":"Miller index [h,k,l].","items":{"type":"integer"},"maxItems":3,"minItems":3,"type":"array"},"output_root":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string"},{"type":"null"}],"default":null,"description":"Directory to write the slab structures. Required for bulk_dir; defaults to 'slabs' for single file. For bulk_dir, outputs are written under output_root/<slab_id>/..., where slab_id encodes the relative input path (without suffix) using '__'."},"slab_thickness":{"default":12.0,"description":"Target slab thickness (Å).","minimum":0.0,"type":"number"},"vacuum_thickness":{"default":15.0,"description":"Vacuum thickness (Å).","minimum":0.0,"type":"number"},"supercell":{"default":[1,1,1],"description":"Supercell replication [a,b,c] for slab structure after generation.","items":{"type":"integer"},"maxItems":3,"minItems":3,"type":"array"},"get_symmetry_slab":{"default":false,"description":"If true, returned slabs will ensure top and bottom surfaces are identical. Use it for surface energy calculation.","type":"boolean"},"orthogonal":{"default":false,"description":"If true, convert each slab to an orthogonal c-oriented cell. Useful for grain boundary generation.","type":"boolean"},"lll_reduce":{"default":false,"description":"Apply LLL reduction during slab generation. Not recommended to use unless necessary.","type":"boolean"}},"required":["miller_index"],"type":"object","additionalProperties":false}}},{"type":"function","function":{"name":"fix_atoms_by_layers","description":"Fix (freeze) the bottom N atomic layers of slab structure(s).\n\n    Provide exactly one of structure_ref or structure_dir. When structure_dir is used, output_dir is required.\n    Batch outputs are written to output_dir/<slab_id>.vasp and a summary JSON is written to\n    output_dir/batch_fix_atoms_by_layers.json.","parameters":{"properties":{"structure_ref":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string"},{"type":"null"}],"default":null,"description":"Slab structure file to modify (POSCAR/CIF)."},"structure_dir":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string"},{"type":"null"}],"default":null,"description":"Directory containing slab structure files to modify."},"output_path":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string"},{"type":"null"}],"default":null,"description":"Output structure path (workspace-relative) for single file."},"output_dir":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string"},{"type":"null"}],"default":null,"description":"Output directory for batch mode. Outputs are written as <output_dir>/<slab_id>.vasp where slab_id encodes the relative input path (without suffix) using '__'."},"freeze_layers":{"description":"Number of bottom layers to freeze. Use layer_tol to group layers.","minimum":0,"type":"integer"},"centralize":{"default":false,"description":"Recentre slab along c before applying constraints.","type":"boolean"},"layer_tol":{"default":0.2,"description":"Layer grouping tolerance in Å. 0.2 is suitable for most cases except for highly tilted slabs.","exclusiveMinimum":0.0,"type":"number"}},"required":["freeze_layers"],"type":"object","additionalProperties":false}}},{"type":"function","function":{"name":"fix_atoms_by_height","description":"Fix (freeze) atoms within specified z ranges of slab structure(s).\n\n    Provide exactly one of structure_ref or structure_dir. When structure_dir is used, output_dir is required.\n    Batch outputs are written to output_dir/<slab_id>.vasp and a summary JSON is written to\n    output_dir/batch_fix_atoms_by_height.json.","parameters":{"properties":{"structure_ref":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string"},{"type":"null"}],"default":null,"description":"Slab structure file to modify (POSCAR/CIF)."},"structure_dir":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string"},{"type":"null"}],"default":null,"description":"Directory containing slab structure files to modify."},"output_path":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string"},{"type":"null"}],"default":null,"description":"Output structure path (workspace-relative) for single file."},"output_dir":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string"},{"type":"null"}],"default":null,"description":"Output directory for batch mode. Outputs are written as <output_dir>/<slab_id>.vasp where slab_id encodes the relative input path (without suffix) using '__'."},"z_ranges":{"description":"Ranges in Å in Cartesian coordinates; atoms in these z ranges are frozen.","items":{"properties":{"z_min":{"description":"Lower bound (Å) in Cartesian coordinates.","type":"number"},"z_max":{"description":"Upper bound (Å) in Cartesian coordinates.","type":"number"}},"required":["z_min","z_max"],"type":"object","additionalProperties":false},"minItems":1,"type":"array"},"centralize":{"default":false,"description":"Recentre slab along c after applying constraints.","type":"boolean"}},"required":["z_ranges"],"type":"object","additionalProperties":false}}},{"type":"function","function":{"name":"supercell","description":"Create supercells from structure file(s). THIS WILL LOSE ALL SELECTIVE DYNAMICS INFORMATION.\n    Provide exactly one of structure_file or structure_dir. When structure_dir is used, output_dir is required.\n    Batch outputs are written to output_dir/<structure_id>.vasp and a summary JSON is written to\n    output_dir/batch_supercell.json.\n\n    The JSON format is:\n    {\n      \"results\": [\n        {\"input_rel\": \"a/CO.vasp\", \"structure_id\": \"a__CO\", \"output_rel\": \"out/a__CO.vasp\", \"natoms\": 2}\n      ]\n    }","parameters":{"properties":{"structure_file":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string"},{"type":"null"}],"default":null,"description":"Bulk structure file (POSCAR/CIF/etc.), workspace-relative."},"structure_dir":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string"},{"type":"null"}],"default":null,"description":"Directory containing structure files for batch supercell generation."},"supercell":{"description":"Supercell replication [a,b,c].","items":{"type":"integer"},"maxItems":3,"minItems":3,"type":"array"},"output_path":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string"},{"type":"null"}],"default":null,"description":"Output structure path for single structure (workspace-relative, e.g., bulk_supercell.vasp)."},"output_dir":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string"},{"type":"null"}],"default":null,"description":"Output directory for batch mode. Outputs are written as <output_dir>/<structure_id>.vasp where structure_id encodes the relative input path (without suffix) using '__'."}},"required":["supercell"],"type":"object","additionalProperties":false}}},{"type":"function","function":{"name":"enumerate_adsorption_sites","description":"Enumerate adsorption sites on a slab using ASF. Use it only for small scale placement.\n\n    The tool writes a JSON list to output_json:\n    [\n      {\"label\": \"ontop_0\", \"kind\": \"ontop\", \"cart_coords\": [x, y, z]}\n    ]\n    The returned tool data includes the workspace-relative path in \"sites\" and \"sites_json_rel\".","parameters":{"properties":{"slab_file":{"description":"Slab structure file (POSCAR/CONTCAR/CIF), workspace-relative.","type":"string"},"mode":{"default":"all","description":"Which site families to return: all|ontop|bridge|hollow.","type":"string"},"distance":{"default":2.0,"description":"Height above surface to sample adsorption sites (Å).","minimum":0.0,"type":"number"},"output_json":{"default":"adsorption/sites.json","description":"Output JSON path for site list (workspace-relative).","type":"string"}},"required":["slab_file"],"type":"object","additionalProperties":false}}},{"type":"function","function":{"name":"place_adsorbate","description":"Place an adsorbate molecule on a slab. Use it only if for small scale placement.\n    This tool keeps selective dynamics of the original slab structure and allows adsorbate to move freely.\n    It writes metadata sidecar <output>.meta.json and an ads_indices index JSON.","parameters":{"properties":{"slab_file":{"description":"Slab structure file (POSCAR/CONTCAR/CIF).","type":"string"},"adsorbate_file":{"description":"Adsorbate molecule file (XYZ).","type":"string"},"site":{"default":"auto","description":"Site label like ontop_0|bridge_1|hollow_2 or 'auto' (which use all[0]).","type":"string"},"distance":{"default":2.0,"description":"Height used to generate adsorption sites (Å).","minimum":0.0,"type":"number"},"output_poscar":{"default":"adsorption/adsorbed.vasp","description":"Output POSCAR path (workspace-relative).","type":"string"}},"required":["slab_file","adsorbate_file"],"type":"object","additionalProperties":false}}},{"type":"function","function":{"name":"generate_batch_adsorption_structures","description":"Generate multiple adsorbed structures up to max_structures. Suitable for large scale placement.\n    This tool keeps selective dynamics of the original slab structure and allows adsorbate to move freely.\n    Input can be a single slab file (slab_file) or a directory of slab files (slab_dir).\n    When slab_dir is used, each slab gets its own subdirectory under output_dir. Max_structures applies per slab.\n    For nested slab_dir layouts, slab_id encodes the relative path (without suffix) using '__'.\n\n    The tool writes a JSON list to output_dir/batch_structures.json and a per-structure\n    metadata sidecar <output>.meta.json with ads_indices.\n    It also writes output_dir/ads_indices.json as an index file:\n    [\n      {\n        \"slab_file_rel\": \"slabs/fe111.vasp\",\n        \"slab_id\": \"fe111\",\n        \"label\": \"ontop_0\",\n        \"output_poscar_rel\": \"adsorption/batch/fe111/ontop_0.vasp\",\n        \"ads_indices_added\": [36],\n        \"ads_indices\": [36]\n      }\n    ]\n    The returned tool data replaces \"structures\" with the workspace-relative path to this JSON file.","parameters":{"properties":{"slab_file":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string"},{"type":"null"}],"default":null,"description":"Slab structure file (POSCAR/CONTCAR/CIF)."},"slab_dir":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string"},{"type":"null"}],"default":null,"description":"Directory containing slab files for high-throughput placement."},"adsorbate_file":{"description":"Adsorbate molecule file (XYZ).","type":"string"},"mode":{"default":"all","description":"all|ontop|bridge|hollow","type":"string"},"distance":{"default":2.0,"description":"Height used to generate adsorption sites (Å).","minimum":0.0,"type":"number"},"max_structures":{"default":1000,"description":"Maximum number of adsorbed structures to generate.","minimum":1,"type":"integer"},"output_dir":{"default":"adsorption/batch","description":"Directory to write batch POSCARs.","type":"string"}},"required":["adsorbate_file"],"type":"object","additionalProperties":false}}},{"type":"function","function":{"name":"make_neb_geometry","description":"Generate NEB interpolation geometries in nebmake.pl style.\n\n    The tool validates that initial and final structures have the same element order, atom count,\n    and lattice (within tolerance). Images are written under output_dir/00..(NI+1) with output_filename.\n    Selective dynamics constraints are preserved if present in the input files (ASE handles constraints).","parameters":{"properties":{"initial_path":{"description":"Initial structure file (POSCAR/CONTCAR/.vasp/.cif).","type":"string"},"final_path":{"description":"Final structure file (POSCAR/CONTCAR/.vasp/.cif).","type":"string"},"n_images":{"description":"Number of intermediate images (NI).","minimum":1,"type":"integer"},"output_dir":{"default":"neb_images","description":"Output directory for image folders (workspace-relative).","type":"string"},"output_filename":{"default":"POSCAR","description":"Filename for each image output (e.g., POSCAR).","type":"string"},"interp_mode":{"default":"direct","description":"Output coordinate style when writing POSCAR: direct (fractional) or cartesian.","pattern":"^(direct|cartesian)$","type":"string"},"interp_method":{"default":"linear","description":"Interpolation method: linear or idpp.","pattern":"^(linear|idpp)$","type":"string"},"vtst_wrap":{"default":true,"description":"If true, wrap fractional coordinates into [0,1) before interpolation (VTST nebmake.pl behavior).","type":"boolean"},"overwrite":{"default":false,"description":"If true, overwrite output_dir if it exists.","type":"boolean"}},"required":["initial_path","final_path","n_images"],"type":"object","additionalProperties":false}}},{"type":"function","function":{"name":"make_neb_incar","description":"Generate a VTST NEB/CI-NEB INCAR based on a template INCAR.\n\n    The tool parses the template INCAR (ignores comments/blank lines, case-insensitive keys),\n    applies NEB overrides, and writes the final INCAR along with a patch JSON.","parameters":{"properties":{"template_incar_path":{"description":"Template INCAR path (workspace-relative).","type":"string"},"output_incar_path":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string"},{"type":"null"}],"default":null,"description":"Output INCAR path. If omitted, uses output_dir/INCAR."},"output_dir":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string"},{"type":"null"}],"default":"neb_inputs","description":"Output directory for INCAR and patch JSON (workspace-relative)."},"images":{"description":"Number of intermediate images (IMAGES).","minimum":1,"type":"integer"},"climb":{"default":false,"description":"Enable CI-NEB with LCLIMB=.TRUE. if true.","type":"boolean"},"iopt":{"default":7,"description":"IOPT value for VTST optimizer (allowed: 7/2/1).","type":"integer"},"ediff":{"anyOf":[{"type":"number"},{"type":"null"}],"default":null,"description":"Override EDIFF if provided."},"ediffg":{"anyOf":[{"type":"number"},{"type":"null"}],"default":null,"description":"Override EDIFFG if provided."},"spring":{"anyOf":[{"type":"number"},{"type":"null"}],"default":null,"description":"Override SPRING if provided."},"potim":{"anyOf":[{"type":"number"},{"type":"null"}],"default":0.0,"description":"Override POTIM (default 0)."},"additional_overrides":{"additionalProperties":true,"description":"Additional INCAR overrides as a dict; highest priority and can override required defaults. In this tool, due to pymatgen constraints, MAGMOM/LDAUU/LDAUJ must be provided as symbol:value maps. If not provided, no user override is applied and this tool's default INCAR strategy is used. Use null value to remove a key from INCAR.","type":"object"}},"required":["template_incar_path","images"],"type":"object","additionalProperties":false}}},{"type":"function","function":{"name":"vasp_execute_batch","description":"Submit VASP runs in one DPDispatcher submission (single-folder or recursive batch modes).","parameters":{"properties":{"input_dir":{"description":"Input directory for VASP execution. Two modes are supported: (1) single-folder mode: input_dir itself is a VASP calc folder containing INCAR and POTCAR; (2) batch mode: recursively discover subfolders containing INCAR and POTCAR. Nested mode is forbidden when input_dir itself is a calc folder and descendants also contain calc folders.","type":"string"},"output_dir":{"description":"Root directory to store outputs. In single-folder mode, results go to output_dir/<basename(input_dir)>. In batch mode, results mirror discovered subfolder layout under output_dir. Must not be inside input_dir. Staging directories under output_dir are cleaned after completion.","type":"string"},"check_interval":{"default":30,"description":"Polling interval seconds","type":"integer"}},"required":["input_dir","output_dir"],"type":"object","additionalProperties":false}}},{"type":"function","function":{"name":"mp_search_materials","description":"Search Materials Project with flexible criteria and write results to CSV.\n\n    Common criteria keys (pass via `criteria`):\n      - material_ids (list[str] or str)\n      - elements (list[str] or str)\n      - chemsys (str)\n      - formula (str)\n      - is_stable (bool)\n      - energy_above_hull ([min, max])\n      - formation_energy ([min, max])\n      - band_gap ([min, max])\n      - crystal_system (str)\n      - spacegroup_number / spacegroup_symbol\n      - num_sites ([min, max])\n      - density ([min, max])\n      - volume ([min, max])\n      - num_elements ([min, max])\n    Common fields for output rows (pass via `fields`):\n      material_id, formula_pretty (or formula), energy_above_hull, formation_energy_per_atom (or formation_energy),\n      band_gap, crystal_system, spacegroup_number, spacegroup_symbol, nsites (or num_sites), density, volume.","parameters":{"properties":{"criteria":{"additionalProperties":true,"description":"Direct summary.search filters as a dict (keys listed above). Range values may be [min, max].","type":"object"},"fields":{"description":"Fields to include in CSV rows; supports common aliases.","items":{"type":"string"},"type":"array"},"limit":{"default":50,"description":"Maximum number of hits to return (default 50).","minimum":1,"type":"integer"},"output_csv":{"description":"Workspace-relative CSV path to write search results.","type":"string"}},"required":["output_csv"],"type":"object","additionalProperties":false}}},{"type":"function","function":{"name":"mp_download_structure","description":"Download one or more structures from Materials Project into the workspace.","parameters":{"properties":{"mp_ids":{"description":"Materials Project IDs, e.g., ['mp-149', 'mp-13'].","items":{"type":"string"},"type":"array"},"fmt":{"default":"poscar","description":"Output format: poscar|cif|json.","pattern":"^(poscar|cif|json)$","type":"string"},"output_dir":{"default":"retrieval/mp","description":"Workspace-relative directory to save the structure.","type":"string"}},"required":["mp_ids"],"type":"object","additionalProperties":false}}},{"type":"function","function":{"name":"bash_exec","description":"Execute a multi-line bash script inside the workspace (default) and return stdout/stderr.\n    Network access is disabled by default using Linux network namespaces (unshare).\n    Symbolic link operations are disabled; use copy/move operations instead.\n    Stdout/stderr are returned as-is and projection/offload is handled centrally.\n    Keep output short in scripts and print one-line summaries when possible.","parameters":{"properties":{"script":{"description":"Bash script to execute (multi-line).","type":"string"},"cwd":{"default":".","description":"Working directory inside project files root.","type":"string"},"timeout_s":{"default":86400.0,"description":"Timeout seconds.","minimum":0.1,"type":"number"},"no_network":{"default":true,"description":"Disable network using unshare network namespace.","type":"boolean"}},"required":["script"],"type":"object","additionalProperties":false}}},{"type":"function","function":{"name":"apply_aider_edits","description":"Apply Aider SEARCH/REPLACE edit blocks to workspace files.","parameters":{"properties":{"edits_text":{"description":"Aider SEARCH/REPLACE edit blocks text. Format per block:\n<relative/path/to/file>\n<<<<<<< SEARCH\n... exact existing text ...\n=======\n... replacement text ...\n>>>>>>> REPLACE","type":"string"},"allowed_paths":{"description":"Optional project-files-relative path prefixes. Use [] to allow edits anywhere under workspace root.","items":{"type":"string"},"type":"array"},"emit_diff":{"default":true,"description":"Whether to return unified diff text for audit.","type":"boolean"}},"required":["edits_text"],"type":"object","additionalProperties":false}}},{"type":"function","function":{"name":"read_text_file","description":"Read the complete contents of a file from the file system as text. Handles various text encodings and provides detailed error messages if the file cannot be read. Use this tool when you need to examine the contents of a single file. Use the 'head' parameter to read only the first N lines of a file, or the 'tail' parameter to read only the last N lines of a file. Operates on the file as text regardless of extension. Only works within allowed directories.","parameters":{"$schema":"http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#","type":"object","properties":{"path":{"type":"string"},"tail":{"description":"If provided, returns only the last N lines of the file","type":"number"},"head":{"description":"If provided, returns only the first N lines of the file","type":"number"}},"required":["path"]}}},{"type":"function","function":{"name":"read_multiple_files","description":"Read the contents of multiple files simultaneously. This is more efficient than reading files one by one when you need to analyze or compare multiple files. Each file's content is returned with its path as a reference. Failed reads for individual files won't stop the entire operation. Only works within allowed directories.","parameters":{"$schema":"http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#","type":"object","properties":{"paths":{"minItems":1,"type":"array","items":{"type":"string"},"description":"Array of file paths to read. Each path must be a string pointing to a valid file within allowed directories."}},"required":["paths"]}}},{"type":"function","function":{"name":"write_file","description":"Create a new file or completely overwrite an existing file with new content. Use with caution as it will overwrite existing files without warning. Handles text content with proper encoding. Only works within allowed directories.","parameters":{"$schema":"http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#","type":"object","properties":{"path":{"type":"string"},"content":{"type":"string"}},"required":["path","content"]}}},{"type":"function","function":{"name":"edit_file","description":"Make line-based edits to a text file. Each edit replaces exact line sequences with new content. Returns a git-style diff showing the changes made. Only works within allowed directories.","parameters":{"$schema":"http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#","type":"object","properties":{"path":{"type":"string"},"edits":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"object","properties":{"oldText":{"type":"string","description":"Text to search for - must match exactly"},"newText":{"type":"string","description":"Text to replace with"}},"required":["oldText","newText"]}},"dryRun":{"default":false,"description":"Preview changes using git-style diff format","type":"boolean"}},"required":["path","edits"]}}},{"type":"function","function":{"name":"create_directory","description":"Create a new directory or ensure a directory exists. Can create multiple nested directories in one operation. If the directory already exists, this operation will succeed silently. Perfect for setting up directory structures for projects or ensuring required paths exist. Only works within allowed directories.","parameters":{"$schema":"http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#","type":"object","properties":{"path":{"type":"string"}},"required":["path"]}}},{"type":"function","function":{"name":"list_directory","description":"Get a detailed listing of all files and directories in a specified path. Results clearly distinguish between files and directories with [FILE] and [DIR] prefixes. This tool is essential for understanding directory structure and finding specific files within a directory. Only works within allowed directories.","parameters":{"$schema":"http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#","type":"object","properties":{"path":{"type":"string"}},"required":["path"]}}},{"type":"function","function":{"name":"directory_tree","description":"Get a recursive tree view of files and directories as a JSON structure. Each entry includes 'name', 'type' (file/directory), and 'children' for directories. Files have no children array, while directories always have a children array (which may be empty). The output is formatted with 2-space indentation for readability. Only works within allowed directories.","parameters":{"$schema":"http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#","type":"object","properties":{"path":{"type":"string"},"excludePatterns":{"default":[],"type":"array","items":{"type":"string"}}},"required":["path"]}}},{"type":"function","function":{"name":"move_file","description":"Move or rename files and directories. Can move files between directories and rename them in a single operation. If the destination exists, the operation will fail. Works across different directories and can be used for simple renaming within the same directory. Both source and destination must be within allowed directories.","parameters":{"$schema":"http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#","type":"object","properties":{"source":{"type":"string"},"destination":{"type":"string"}},"required":["source","destination"]}}},{"type":"function","function":{"name":"search_files","description":"Recursively search for files and directories matching a pattern. The patterns should be glob-style patterns that match paths relative to the working directory. Use pattern like '*.ext' to match files in current directory, and '**/*.ext' to match files in all subdirectories. Returns full paths to all matching items. Great for finding files when you don't know their exact location. Only searches within allowed directories.","parameters":{"$schema":"http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#","type":"object","properties":{"path":{"type":"string"},"pattern":{"type":"string"},"excludePatterns":{"default":[],"type":"array","items":{"type":"string"}}},"required":["path","pattern"]}}},{"type":"function","function":{"name":"TaskOutput","description":"Structured output from the task runner agent.","parameters":{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"status":{"description":"Task terminal status. Use 'done' only when task acceptance criteria are satisfied; use 'blocked' when progress is blocked by unresolved issues.","enum":["done","blocked"],"type":"string"},"summary":{"description":"Concise task outcome/failure summary with key file pointers. Do not paste long tables/logs/scripts; cite file paths instead.","type":"string"},"facts":{"description":"Only high-value verified facts reusable downstream (include units/conditions/evidence path when relevant). Do not restate command traces. Use [] when none.","items":{"type":"string"},"type":"array"},"files":{"description":"Only key reproducibility/user-facing artifact paths (files or directories). Use a directory path when it is a clearer bundle-level reference. Avoid listing low-value scratch files. Use [] when none.","items":{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"path":{"description":"Workspace-relative artifact path (file or directory). Always use project-relative paths; do not use absolute paths.","type":"string"},"description":{"description":"Short one-line description.","type":"string"},"kind":{"description":"Artifact category. Common values: script, output, report, log. Use 'dir' when the path points to a directory bundle.","type":"string"}},"required":["path","description","kind"],"type":"object"},"type":"array"},"constraints":{"description":"Only new/changed constraints. Use [] when none.","items":{"type":"string"},"type":"array"},"open_questions":{"description":"Only unresolved blockers affecting next steps. Do not include speculative questions. Use [] when none.","items":{"type":"string"},"type":"array"},"decisions":{"description":"Only decisions materially affecting downstream work; avoid duplicating summary/facts content. Use [] when none.","items":{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"decision":{"description":"Short decision statement.","type":"string"},"rationale":{"description":"Brief rationale (one short sentence preferred).","type":"string"}},"required":["decision","rationale"],"type":"object"},"type":"array"},"next_steps":{"description":"Only immediate actionable next steps. Use [] when no next step is required.","items":{"type":"string"},"type":"array"},"artifacts":{"description":"Supporting artifact paths when needed. Use [] when none.","items":{"type":"string"},"type":"array"},"error":{"description":"Failure reason for status=blocked. For status=done, use empty string ''.","type":"string"},"needs_human":{"description":"Whether a human must intervene for status=blocked. For status=done, set false.","type":"boolean"},"hint":{"description":"Optional concise recovery hint for status=blocked. For status=done, use empty string ''.","type":"string"}},"required":["status","summary","facts","files","constraints","open_questions","decisions","next_steps","artifacts","error","needs_human","hint"],"type":"object"}}}],"prompt_cache_retention":"24h"}
17:22:30 INFO httpx | HTTP Request: POST https://openrouter.ai/api/v1/chat/completions "HTTP/1.1 200 OK"
17:22:40 INFO catmaster.llm.factory | [llm.http.raw_post] provider=openrouter model=openai/gpt-5.3-codex:online method=POST url=https://openrouter.ai/api/v1/chat/completions body={"messages":[{"content":"You are an execution controller. Use tool calling to advance the current task.\n\nPriority rules:\n- Use tool calling from all available tools to achieve the goal in the context pack.\n- Check tool names and params carefully.\n- Treat memory index as cross-run historical memory from prior decisions/scientific invariant updates and it may lag current-run progress.\n- For current execution, task packet (goal/detail/expected outputs) is authoritative; use memory for reusable invariants and prior-run context only.\n- Task detail defines the task invariants and done checks. Execute with the minimal non-destructive procedure that satisfies those invariants. Treat task-detail parameters as preferred unless explicitly marked hard, and do bounded self-adjustments before escalating while keeping scientific/computational invariants fixed.\n- Tool schemas are authoritative for argument shapes/defaults; do not re-invent parameter templates in bash scripts.\n- Do not initiate file edits on your own. Only edit files when the current task packet explicitly requires editing/writing outputs for this task. For `MEMORY/**`, only update when scientific invariants, method definitions, or final reusable results changed.\n- If file editing is explicitly required by the task packet, prefer `apply_aider_edits` for deterministic edits (including memory files) over ad-hoc in-place shell edits.\n\nExecution rules:\n- Do not rerun the same preparation tool with identical parameters if the previous call already succeeded and required artifacts still exist. Prefer reusing and validating existing outputs.\n- Do not trigger expensive reruns purely for path/layout normalization when numerical/physical requirements are already satisfied.\n- Bundle independent filesystem operations in the same turn whenever possible, but do not issue concurrent write calls; keep write/edit/move/create operations sequential and verify each write step before the next.\n- For simple multi-directory setup or one-shot workspace reconnaissance, prefer a single focused bash_exec over many single-path filesystem tool calls.\n- Perform only checks required to satisfy current done criteria; avoid speculative or perfection-oriented extra validation.\n- For routine checks, keep bash output small: prefer focused queries (`rg -n`, `head`, `tail`) and avoid broad/full-file dumps unless deep debugging is required.\n- Prefer read_multiple_files when you need several small text files at once.\n- Progressive disclosure is mandatory: memory_index_excerpt is short; discover paths with `search_files` / `list_directory` / `directory_tree`, then read small windows via `read_text_file(head=..., tail=...)`.\n- Use `bash_exec` for shell execution, content grep (`rg`), parser invocation, and external binaries.\n- Internal metadata audit logs are not task inputs; do not read or reference them in task reasoning.\n- By default, do not generate long markdown reports via `cat <<'MD'`.\n\nParsing policy:\n- Debug triage should prioritize focused, minimal evidence extraction and concise failure signatures.\n- For extracting final numerical results across many calculations (for comparison/reporting), avoid repeated manual grep stitching; prefer parser libraries or small single-purpose scripts.\n- Prefer mature third-party libraries for parsing and post-analysis when available; avoid reimplementing standard parsers/analysis logic from scratch.\n- Common Python packages are available and preferred when relevant: ase, pymatgen, numpy, matplotlib, scipy, pandas, fitz, requests.\n- For actual workload execution (batch processing, long runs, or outputs to be reused/audited), write reusable script files and keep each script focused/small.\n\nTermination and handoff:\n- End with one concise final handoff that clearly states the task status and reusable outputs.\n- Use `status=\"done\"` when task is complete.\n- Use `status=\"blocked\"` only when still blocked after bounded self-adjustment attempts on non-critical execution parameters, or when hard scientific invariants conflict.\n- Follow schema field descriptions for per-field content quality and placeholders; do not fill fields with invented content.\n- For remote/batch job failures, do one minimal triage (failing status file, stdout/stderr snippets, key inputs) and attempt one focused fix.\n- Do not do open-ended exploration for remote failures (no SSH). If failure persists, return `status=\"blocked\"` with failed paths, evidence pointers, likely cause, and a minimal rerun/repair plan that reruns only the failed subset.\n- Keep handoff evidence-based and concise; avoid redundant repetition across fields.\n- Function tools must be invoked via tool calls. Do NOT put function tool names into bash_exec commands.\n- Keep stdout concise; if persistent command logs are needed, use pipeline logging to project files (e.g., `cmd 2>&1 | tee reports/<task_desc>/run.log`) and print short summaries.\n- Always provide file or directory paths as relative paths; they will be resolved relative to the project files root.\n","role":"system"},{"content":"<context_pack>\nTask goal:\nRun a VASP relaxation for gas-phase O2 in a large cubic box and extract final energy/atom and O–O bond length.\n\nTask detail:\n1) Create a new workdir `o2_vasp/relax/`.\n2) Build O2 geometry (SMILES `O=O`) and place in a cubic cell with ~15–20 Å vacuum (e.g., 18 Å) centered; write a structure file usable by VASP prep (POSCAR or an intermediate format your prep tool accepts).\n3) Prepare VASP relaxation inputs from scratch in that folder (INCAR/KPOINTS/POSCAR/POTCAR) using PBE PAW for O. Use Gamma-only KPOINTS 1x1x1. Use spin-polarization for triplet O2 (ISPIN=2; initialize MAGMOM ~1 1 and/or set NUPDOWN=2). Recommend: PREC=Accurate, ENCUT=520 (or >= POTCAR ENMAX), EDIFF=1e-6, EDIFFG=-0.02, ISMEAR=0 SIGMA=0.05, IBRION=2, NSW=100, ISIF=2, ISYM=0, LCHARG=.FALSE., LWAVE=.FALSE.\n4) Execute VASP in that directory (single job) until convergence. Ensure outputs include OUTCAR, OSZICAR, CONTCAR.\n5) Parse results: (a) final TOTEN from OUTCAR (last ionic step) and compute energy per atom = TOTEN/2 in eV/atom; (b) compute O–O distance from CONTCAR final positions (Å).\n6) Write a short `o2_vasp/RESULTS.md` summarizing: settings used, final energy (eV), energy/atom (eV/atom), bond length (Å), and point to evidence lines/paths (e.g., OUTCAR grep output, CONTCAR).\n\nExpected outputs:\n- Directory `o2_vasp/relax/` containing INCAR, KPOINTS, POSCAR, POTCAR, and VASP outputs (OUTCAR, OSZICAR, CONTCAR).\n- `o2_vasp/RESULTS.md` with final TOTEN (eV), energy per atom (eV/atom), and O–O bond length (Å) plus file/line references or extracted snippets.\n\nSuggested tools:\ncreate_molecule_from_smiles, vasp_relax_prepare, vasp_execute_batch, bash_exec, read_text_file, write_file\n\nReference hint:\n- If `vasp_relax_prepare` needs a structure file, generate an XYZ first then convert/write POSCAR.\n- Use `grep -n \"free  energy   TOTEN\" OUTCAR | tail -1` to capture final TOTEN line.\n- Bond length: parse CONTCAR (Cartesian) and compute distance between the two atoms via a tiny python snippet in bash.\n\nWorkspace policy:\nProject files policy:\n- Treat \".\" as the project files root.\n- All path parameters and returned paths are relative to \".\".\n- Never use absolute paths or metadata paths.\n- Use search_files / list_directory / directory_tree to discover files.\n- Use read_text_file with head/tail for progressive disclosure.\n- Use bash_exec for shell commands, content grep, parser invocation, and external binaries.\n- Role: task_runner\n\nMemory index excerpt:\n# MEMORY (AUTOLOADED INDEX)\n\n## What this is\n- Autoloaded memory index for this project.\n- Keep this file concise and pointer-first.\n- Put details in MEMORY/topics/*.md.\n\n## Latest State\n- Current focus: Compute O2 in a box: prepare VASP inputs from scratch, DO perform VASP calculation to get the results, and report final energy per atom and O–O bond distance from vasp results.\n- Current milestone: (empty)\n- Latest run artifact: (empty)\n- Next action: (empty)\n\n## Top Constraints\n1. (empty)\n\n## Active Open Questions\n1. (empty)\n\n## Pointers\n- Facts / decisions: MEMORY/topics/FACTS.md\n- Files / artifacts: MEMORY/topics/FILES.md\n- Constraints: MEMORY/topics/CONSTRAINTS.md\n- Open questions: MEMORY/topics/QUESTIONS.md\n- Runbook: MEMORY/topics/RUNBOOK.md\n\n## Keyword Map\n- GOAL: objective, success criteria, scope, non-goals\n- FACTS: definition, verified, result, decision\n- FILES: path, artifact, dataset, output, script\n- CONSTRAINTS: must, cannot, policy, budget\n- QUESTIONS: unknown, blocked, clarify, decide\n- RUNBOOK: steps, checklist, verify\n\n</context_pack>\n","role":"user"},{"content":null,"role":"assistant","tool_calls":[{"type":"function","id":"call_NLAqyx4HYI4uImLrpUJQ3jgo","function":{"name":"bash_exec","arguments":"{\"script\": \"set -e\\nmkdir -p o2_vasp/relax\\nprintf 'created o2_vasp/relax\\\\n'\\nls -la o2_vasp\", \"cwd\": \".\", \"timeout_s\": 120, \"no_network\": true}"}}]},{"content":"stdout:\ncreated o2_vasp/relax\ntotal 12\ndrwxr-xr-x 3 root root 4096 Mar  3 17:21 .\ndrwxr-xr-x 4 root root 4096 Mar  3 17:21 ..\ndrwxr-xr-x 2 root root 4096 Mar  3 17:21 relax\n\nexit_code=0 timed_out=False cancelled=False cwd=. timeout_s=120.0\nOffload: _tool_outputs/bash_exec/bash_exec_20260303T092152947189Z_bf00889a.json","role":"tool","tool_call_id":"call_NLAqyx4HYI4uImLrpUJQ3jgo"},{"content":null,"role":"assistant","tool_calls":[{"type":"function","id":"call_4wr72H1u1SwOyVJwdFqACxhS","function":{"name":"create_molecule_from_smiles","arguments":"{\"smiles\": \"O=O\", \"name\": \"O2\", \"output_path\": \"o2_vasp/relax/o2\", \"box_padding\": 9, \"fmt\": \"both\"}"}}]},{"content":"create_molecule_from_smiles completed.\nformula=O2 natoms=2\nxyz_file_rel=o2_vasp/relax/o2.xyz poscar_file_rel=o2_vasp/relax/o2.vasp","role":"tool","tool_call_id":"call_4wr72H1u1SwOyVJwdFqACxhS"},{"content":null,"role":"assistant","tool_calls":[{"type":"function","id":"call_5jHw8cDeUnGwFibV0EEcXEEN","function":{"name":"vasp_relax_prepare","arguments":"{\"input_path\": \"o2_vasp/relax/o2.vasp\", \"output_root\": \"o2_vasp/relax\", \"calc_type\": \"gas\", \"relax_cell\": false, \"k_product\": 30, \"use_d3\": false, \"use_dft_plus_u\": false, \"compute_dos\": false, \"enable_dipole\": false}"}}]},{"content":"vasp_relax_prepare completed.\nstructures_processed=1 errors_count=0 calc_type=gas\noutput_root_rel=o2_vasp/relax\nfirst_prepared_dir=o2_vasp/relax/o2","role":"tool","tool_call_id":"call_5jHw8cDeUnGwFibV0EEcXEEN"},{"content":null,"role":"assistant","tool_calls":[{"type":"function","id":"call_lHpu2I0UUEw3BsBalLeYGNYu","function":{"name":"bash_exec","arguments":"{\"script\": \"set -e\\nfind o2_vasp -maxdepth 3 -type f | sort\\nprintf '\\\\nINCAR:\\\\n'\\ncat o2_vasp/relax/o2/INCAR\\nprintf '\\\\nKPOINTS:\\\\n'\\ncat o2_vasp/relax/o2/KPOINTS\", \"cwd\": \".\", \"timeout_s\": 120, \"no_network\": true}"}}]},{"content":"stdout:\no2_vasp/relax/o2.vasp\no2_vasp/relax/o2.xyz\no2_vasp/relax/o2/INCAR\no2_vasp/relax/o2/KPOINTS\no2_vasp/relax/o2/POSCAR\no2_vasp/relax/o2/POTCAR\n\nINCAR:\nALGO = Fast\nEDIFF = 1e-06\nEDIFFG = -0.02\nENCUT = 520.0\nIBRION = 2\nISIF = 2\nISMEAR = 0\nISPIN = 2\nISYM = 0\nLASPH = True\nLCHARG = False\nLDAU = False\nLORBIT = 0\nLREAL = False\nLWAVE = False\nMAGMOM = 2*0.6\nNELM = 100\nNSW = 500\nPREC = Accurate\nSIGMA = 0.01\n\nKPOINTS:\nAutomatic kpoint scheme\n0\nGamma\n1 1 1\n\nexit_code=0 timed_out=False cancelled=False cwd=. timeout_s=120.0\nOffload: _tool_outputs/bash_exec/bash_exec_20260303T092230287978Z_9794df37.json","role":"tool","tool_call_id":"call_lHpu2I0UUEw3BsBalLeYGNYu"},{"content":null,"role":"assistant","tool_calls":[{"type":"function","id":"call_xjgGq0wmm5vnOJC5ChKpKOCp","function":{"name":"read_text_file","arguments":"{\"path\": \"o2_vasp/relax/o2/POSCAR\", \"tail\": 40, \"head\": 0}"}}]},{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"O2\n1.0\n  19.1509299999999989    0.0000000000000000    0.0000000000000000\n   0.0000000000000000   19.1509299999999989    0.0000000000000000\n   0.0000000000000000    0.0000000000000000   19.1509299999999989\nO\n2\ndirect\n   0.5300489323494995    0.4999999999999999    0.4999999999999999 O\n   0.4699510676505005    0.4999999999999999    0.4999999999999999 O\n","id":"lc_1bc5653c-3730-427d-8a78-472bf42ce177"}],"role":"tool","tool_call_id":"call_xjgGq0wmm5vnOJC5ChKpKOCp"}],"model":"openai/gpt-5.3-codex:online","reasoning_effort":"medium","stream":false,"temperature":1.0,"tool_choice":"required","tools":[{"type":"function","function":{"name":"create_molecule_from_smiles","description":"Build a 3D molecule from a SMILES string using RDKit. Specially, pay attention to the formal charge of the SMILES string, RDkit will check the charge and add Hs to the molecule to make it neutral.","parameters":{"properties":{"smiles":{"description":"SMILES string for the molecule.","type":"string"},"name":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string"},{"type":"null"}],"default":null,"description":"Optional base name for output files; defaults to formula."},"output_path":{"default":"mol","description":"Workspace-relative path prefix; files will be <prefix>.xyz and/or <prefix>.vasp.","type":"string"},"box_padding":{"default":10.0,"description":"Padding (Å) added around the molecule to make a cubic box for POSCAR. Box lattice is around twice the padding value (10A Padding -> 20A Box).","minimum":0.0,"type":"number"},"fmt":{"default":"poscar","description":"Output format: poscar (with PBC box), xyz (no PBC), or both.","pattern":"^(poscar|xyz|both)$","type":"string"}},"required":["smiles"],"type":"object","additionalProperties":false}}},{"type":"function","function":{"name":"mace_relax_batch","description":"Submit multiple MACE relaxations in one DPDispatcher submission. Preferred tool for batch MACE relaxations.","parameters":{"properties":{"input_dir":{"description":"Root directory containing structure files with lattice (POSCAR/CIF).","type":"string"},"output_root":{"description":"Root directory to store batch outputs. Results mirror the input directory structure; each input file expands to a folder without suffix (e.g. input_dir/a/c.vasp -> output_root/a/c/opt.vasp). Must be outside input_dir.","type":"string"},"fmax":{"default":0.02,"description":"Force threshold for relaxation in eV/Angstrom.","exclusiveMinimum":0,"type":"number"},"maxsteps":{"default":500,"description":"Max steps for relaxation.","minimum":1,"type":"integer"},"model":{"default":"mh-1","description":"MACE model name. Recommended options: 'mh-1' (slower, higher accuracy) or 'medium-mpa-0' (faster, lower accuracy).","examples":["mh-1","medium-mpa-0"],"type":"string"},"head":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string"},{"type":"null"}],"default":"omat_pbe","description":"Model head for multi-head models (e.g. 'omat_pbe'). Use empty string to disable."},"dispersion":{"default":false,"description":"Enable dispersion correction in mace_mp. Default: false.","type":"boolean"},"relax_lattice":{"default":false,"description":"Whether to relax lattice/cell together with atomic positions via ASE FrechetCellFilter.","type":"boolean"},"check_interval":{"default":30,"description":"Polling interval in seconds when waiting.","type":"integer"}},"required":["input_dir","output_root"],"type":"object","additionalProperties":false}}},{"type":"function","function":{"name":"mace_sp_batch","description":"Run MACE single-point jobs for structures under one directory.","parameters":{"properties":{"input_dir":{"description":"Input directory containing structures (POSCAR/CONTCAR/CIF/VASP).","type":"string"},"output_root":{"description":"Output root for batch results. Must be outside input_dir.","type":"string"},"model":{"default":"mh-1","description":"MACE model name (e.g., mh-1, medium-mpa-0).","examples":["mh-1","medium-mpa-0"],"type":"string"},"head":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string"},{"type":"null"}],"default":"omat_pbe","description":"Model head for multi-head models. Use empty string to disable."},"dispersion":{"default":false,"description":"Enable dispersion correction.","type":"boolean"},"check_interval":{"default":30,"description":"Polling interval in seconds when waiting.","type":"integer"}},"required":["input_dir","output_root"],"type":"object","additionalProperties":false}}},{"type":"function","function":{"name":"vasp_relax_prepare","description":"Prepare MPRelaxSet-based VASP relax inputs with calc_type presets and k_product k-mesh.\n    Also can be modified for other calculation types by overriding INCAR via the user_incar_settings.\n    Support exts: .vasp, .cif\n\n    Baseline DFT settings follow Materials Project MPRelaxSet (key defaults):\n    - PBE54 POTCARS, ENCUT=520 eV, PREC=Accurate, ISPIN=2, IBRION=2, LREAL=AUTO, LASPH=True, LWAVE=False, LCHARG=False.\n    - Additional overrides applied based on calc_type: ISMEAR=0, SIGMA=0.1 for bulk/slab; ISMEAR=0, SIGMA=0.01 for gas.\n    - ISIF policy: bulk with relax_cell=False -> ISIF=2; bulk with relax_cell=True -> ISIF=3.\n      slab and gas always use ISIF=2, where slab forces KPOINTS z=1 and gas forces KPOINTS 1x1x1 with ISYM=0, LREAL=False.\n    - Improved convergence settings: EDIFF=1e-6; NSW=500; EDIFFG=-0.02;\n    - LORBIT is controlled by compute_dos (default False -> LORBIT=0, True -> LORBIT=11).\n    - KPOINTS is generated by k*a=k_product, where a is the lattice constant in Angstrom. Set to 30 by default and sufficient for most systems.\n    - DFT-D3 and DFT+U are disabled by default. Enable them if the system is adsorption system(DFT-D3) or transition metal oxide system(DFT+U).","parameters":{"properties":{"input_path":{"description":"Path to a structure file with lattice information (POSCAR/CIF) or a directory containing multiple structures. Support exts: .vasp, .cif","type":"string"},"output_root":{"description":"Root directory for generated VASP inputs (one subfolder per input structure). If input_path is a file: output_root/<stem>/...; if input_path is a directory, preserve relative subfolders: output_root/<relpath>/<stem>/...","type":"string"},"calc_type":{"default":"bulk","description":"Calculation type: 'gas'|'bulk'|'slab'. This provides preset INCAR overrides for different calculation types. gas is suitable for small molecules; slab is suitable for surface slab models; bulk is suitable for bulk relaxations.","enum":["gas","bulk","slab"],"type":"string"},"relax_cell":{"default":false,"description":"Whether to relax cell shape/volume (ISIF=3). Only valid when calc_type='bulk'.","type":"boolean"},"k_product":{"default":30,"description":"Target k-mesh density via k_i~round(k_product/L_i), min 1, forced odd (Gamma-centered); gas always 1x1x1.","minimum":1,"type":"integer"},"use_d3":{"default":false,"description":"Enable DFT-D3 Correction (IVDW=11). Enable it for adsorption calculations.","type":"boolean"},"use_dft_plus_u":{"default":false,"description":"Enable DFT+U relevant settings according to materials project standard. Enable it for Transition Metal Oxide systems.","type":"boolean"},"compute_dos":{"default":false,"description":"Enable DOS/projection output by setting LORBIT=11. Default false (LORBIT=0) to reduce disk usage.","type":"boolean"},"enable_dipole":{"default":false,"description":"Enable dipole correction helper. When true, default IDIPOL=3 and set DIPOL to the atomic center of mass of cell in fractional coordinates.","type":"boolean"},"user_incar_settings":{"additionalProperties":true,"description":"User INCAR overrides as a json object as per pymatgen's user_incar_settings format, e.g. {\"MAGMOM\":{\"O\":1},\"ALGO\":\"Fast\"}. In this tool, due to pymatgen constraints, MAGMOM/LDAUU/LDAUJ must be provided as symbol:value maps. Use null only as a value inside the override object to remove a specific INCAR key, e.g. `{\"LREAL\": null}`. calc_type/task-required presets still take precedence on key conflict.","type":"object"}},"required":["input_path","output_root"],"type":"object","additionalProperties":false}}},{"type":"function","function":{"name":"vasp_sp_prepare","description":"Prepare MPRelaxSet-based VASP single-point inputs for structures under a file or directory. Parameters are the same as VaspRelaxPrepareInput, but with single_point relaxation enabled (NSW=0, IBRION=-1).","parameters":{"properties":{"input_path":{"description":"Structure file or directory of structures. Supported: .vasp, .cif","type":"string"},"output_root":{"description":"Root directory for generated VASP inputs (one subfolder per structure).","type":"string"},"calc_type":{"default":"bulk","description":"Calculation preset for k-mesh and INCAR defaults.","enum":["gas","bulk","slab"],"type":"string"},"k_product":{"default":30,"description":"k-mesh density via k_i~round(k_product/L_i), min 1.","minimum":1,"type":"integer"},"use_d3":{"default":false,"description":"Enable DFT-D3 correction (IVDW=11).","type":"boolean"},"use_dft_plus_u":{"default":false,"description":"Enable DFT+U settings.","type":"boolean"},"compute_dos":{"default":false,"description":"Enable DOS/projection output by setting LORBIT=11. Default false (LORBIT=0).","type":"boolean"},"enable_dipole":{"default":false,"description":"Enable dipole correction helper. When true, default IDIPOL=3 and set DIPOL to the atomic center of mass in fractional coordinates.","type":"boolean"},"user_incar_settings":{"additionalProperties":true,"description":"User INCAR overrides as a json object as per pymatgen's user_incar_settings format, e.g. {\"MAGMOM\":{\"O\":1},\"ALGO\":\"Fast\"}. In this tool, due to pymatgen constraints, MAGMOM/LDAUU/LDAUJ must be provided as symbol:value maps. Use null only as a value inside the override object to remove a specific INCAR key, e.g. `{\"LORBIT\": null}`. calc_type/task-required presets still take precedence on key conflict.","type":"object"}},"required":["input_path","output_root"],"type":"object","additionalProperties":false}}},{"type":"function","function":{"name":"build_slab","description":"Build slabs for all terminations of a Miller index from bulk structure(s).\n\n    Provide exactly one of bulk_structure or bulk_dir. When bulk_dir is used, output_root is required.\n    Batch outputs are written under output_root/<slab_id>/..., where slab_id encodes the relative input path\n    (without suffix) using '__'.","parameters":{"properties":{"bulk_structure":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string"},{"type":"null"}],"default":null,"description":"Bulk structure file (POSCAR/CIF/etc.), workspace-relative."},"bulk_dir":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string"},{"type":"null"}],"default":null,"description":"Directory containing bulk structure files for batch slab building."},"miller_index":{"description":"Miller index [h,k,l].","items":{"type":"integer"},"maxItems":3,"minItems":3,"type":"array"},"output_root":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string"},{"type":"null"}],"default":null,"description":"Directory to write the slab structures. Required for bulk_dir; defaults to 'slabs' for single file. For bulk_dir, outputs are written under output_root/<slab_id>/..., where slab_id encodes the relative input path (without suffix) using '__'."},"slab_thickness":{"default":12.0,"description":"Target slab thickness (Å).","minimum":0.0,"type":"number"},"vacuum_thickness":{"default":15.0,"description":"Vacuum thickness (Å).","minimum":0.0,"type":"number"},"supercell":{"default":[1,1,1],"description":"Supercell replication [a,b,c] for slab structure after generation.","items":{"type":"integer"},"maxItems":3,"minItems":3,"type":"array"},"get_symmetry_slab":{"default":false,"description":"If true, returned slabs will ensure top and bottom surfaces are identical. Use it for surface energy calculation.","type":"boolean"},"orthogonal":{"default":false,"description":"If true, convert each slab to an orthogonal c-oriented cell. Useful for grain boundary generation.","type":"boolean"},"lll_reduce":{"default":false,"description":"Apply LLL reduction during slab generation. Not recommended to use unless necessary.","type":"boolean"}},"required":["miller_index"],"type":"object","additionalProperties":false}}},{"type":"function","function":{"name":"fix_atoms_by_layers","description":"Fix (freeze) the bottom N atomic layers of slab structure(s).\n\n    Provide exactly one of structure_ref or structure_dir. When structure_dir is used, output_dir is required.\n    Batch outputs are written to output_dir/<slab_id>.vasp and a summary JSON is written to\n    output_dir/batch_fix_atoms_by_layers.json.","parameters":{"properties":{"structure_ref":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string"},{"type":"null"}],"default":null,"description":"Slab structure file to modify (POSCAR/CIF)."},"structure_dir":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string"},{"type":"null"}],"default":null,"description":"Directory containing slab structure files to modify."},"output_path":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string"},{"type":"null"}],"default":null,"description":"Output structure path (workspace-relative) for single file."},"output_dir":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string"},{"type":"null"}],"default":null,"description":"Output directory for batch mode. Outputs are written as <output_dir>/<slab_id>.vasp where slab_id encodes the relative input path (without suffix) using '__'."},"freeze_layers":{"description":"Number of bottom layers to freeze. Use layer_tol to group layers.","minimum":0,"type":"integer"},"centralize":{"default":false,"description":"Recentre slab along c before applying constraints.","type":"boolean"},"layer_tol":{"default":0.2,"description":"Layer grouping tolerance in Å. 0.2 is suitable for most cases except for highly tilted slabs.","exclusiveMinimum":0.0,"type":"number"}},"required":["freeze_layers"],"type":"object","additionalProperties":false}}},{"type":"function","function":{"name":"fix_atoms_by_height","description":"Fix (freeze) atoms within specified z ranges of slab structure(s).\n\n    Provide exactly one of structure_ref or structure_dir. When structure_dir is used, output_dir is required.\n    Batch outputs are written to output_dir/<slab_id>.vasp and a summary JSON is written to\n    output_dir/batch_fix_atoms_by_height.json.","parameters":{"properties":{"structure_ref":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string"},{"type":"null"}],"default":null,"description":"Slab structure file to modify (POSCAR/CIF)."},"structure_dir":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string"},{"type":"null"}],"default":null,"description":"Directory containing slab structure files to modify."},"output_path":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string"},{"type":"null"}],"default":null,"description":"Output structure path (workspace-relative) for single file."},"output_dir":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string"},{"type":"null"}],"default":null,"description":"Output directory for batch mode. Outputs are written as <output_dir>/<slab_id>.vasp where slab_id encodes the relative input path (without suffix) using '__'."},"z_ranges":{"description":"Ranges in Å in Cartesian coordinates; atoms in these z ranges are frozen.","items":{"properties":{"z_min":{"description":"Lower bound (Å) in Cartesian coordinates.","type":"number"},"z_max":{"description":"Upper bound (Å) in Cartesian coordinates.","type":"number"}},"required":["z_min","z_max"],"type":"object","additionalProperties":false},"minItems":1,"type":"array"},"centralize":{"default":false,"description":"Recentre slab along c after applying constraints.","type":"boolean"}},"required":["z_ranges"],"type":"object","additionalProperties":false}}},{"type":"function","function":{"name":"supercell","description":"Create supercells from structure file(s). THIS WILL LOSE ALL SELECTIVE DYNAMICS INFORMATION.\n    Provide exactly one of structure_file or structure_dir. When structure_dir is used, output_dir is required.\n    Batch outputs are written to output_dir/<structure_id>.vasp and a summary JSON is written to\n    output_dir/batch_supercell.json.\n\n    The JSON format is:\n    {\n      \"results\": [\n        {\"input_rel\": \"a/CO.vasp\", \"structure_id\": \"a__CO\", \"output_rel\": \"out/a__CO.vasp\", \"natoms\": 2}\n      ]\n    }","parameters":{"properties":{"structure_file":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string"},{"type":"null"}],"default":null,"description":"Bulk structure file (POSCAR/CIF/etc.), workspace-relative."},"structure_dir":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string"},{"type":"null"}],"default":null,"description":"Directory containing structure files for batch supercell generation."},"supercell":{"description":"Supercell replication [a,b,c].","items":{"type":"integer"},"maxItems":3,"minItems":3,"type":"array"},"output_path":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string"},{"type":"null"}],"default":null,"description":"Output structure path for single structure (workspace-relative, e.g., bulk_supercell.vasp)."},"output_dir":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string"},{"type":"null"}],"default":null,"description":"Output directory for batch mode. Outputs are written as <output_dir>/<structure_id>.vasp where structure_id encodes the relative input path (without suffix) using '__'."}},"required":["supercell"],"type":"object","additionalProperties":false}}},{"type":"function","function":{"name":"enumerate_adsorption_sites","description":"Enumerate adsorption sites on a slab using ASF. Use it only for small scale placement.\n\n    The tool writes a JSON list to output_json:\n    [\n      {\"label\": \"ontop_0\", \"kind\": \"ontop\", \"cart_coords\": [x, y, z]}\n    ]\n    The returned tool data includes the workspace-relative path in \"sites\" and \"sites_json_rel\".","parameters":{"properties":{"slab_file":{"description":"Slab structure file (POSCAR/CONTCAR/CIF), workspace-relative.","type":"string"},"mode":{"default":"all","description":"Which site families to return: all|ontop|bridge|hollow.","type":"string"},"distance":{"default":2.0,"description":"Height above surface to sample adsorption sites (Å).","minimum":0.0,"type":"number"},"output_json":{"default":"adsorption/sites.json","description":"Output JSON path for site list (workspace-relative).","type":"string"}},"required":["slab_file"],"type":"object","additionalProperties":false}}},{"type":"function","function":{"name":"place_adsorbate","description":"Place an adsorbate molecule on a slab. Use it only if for small scale placement.\n    This tool keeps selective dynamics of the original slab structure and allows adsorbate to move freely.\n    It writes metadata sidecar <output>.meta.json and an ads_indices index JSON.","parameters":{"properties":{"slab_file":{"description":"Slab structure file (POSCAR/CONTCAR/CIF).","type":"string"},"adsorbate_file":{"description":"Adsorbate molecule file (XYZ).","type":"string"},"site":{"default":"auto","description":"Site label like ontop_0|bridge_1|hollow_2 or 'auto' (which use all[0]).","type":"string"},"distance":{"default":2.0,"description":"Height used to generate adsorption sites (Å).","minimum":0.0,"type":"number"},"output_poscar":{"default":"adsorption/adsorbed.vasp","description":"Output POSCAR path (workspace-relative).","type":"string"}},"required":["slab_file","adsorbate_file"],"type":"object","additionalProperties":false}}},{"type":"function","function":{"name":"generate_batch_adsorption_structures","description":"Generate multiple adsorbed structures up to max_structures. Suitable for large scale placement.\n    This tool keeps selective dynamics of the original slab structure and allows adsorbate to move freely.\n    Input can be a single slab file (slab_file) or a directory of slab files (slab_dir).\n    When slab_dir is used, each slab gets its own subdirectory under output_dir. Max_structures applies per slab.\n    For nested slab_dir layouts, slab_id encodes the relative path (without suffix) using '__'.\n\n    The tool writes a JSON list to output_dir/batch_structures.json and a per-structure\n    metadata sidecar <output>.meta.json with ads_indices.\n    It also writes output_dir/ads_indices.json as an index file:\n    [\n      {\n        \"slab_file_rel\": \"slabs/fe111.vasp\",\n        \"slab_id\": \"fe111\",\n        \"label\": \"ontop_0\",\n        \"output_poscar_rel\": \"adsorption/batch/fe111/ontop_0.vasp\",\n        \"ads_indices_added\": [36],\n        \"ads_indices\": [36]\n      }\n    ]\n    The returned tool data replaces \"structures\" with the workspace-relative path to this JSON file.","parameters":{"properties":{"slab_file":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string"},{"type":"null"}],"default":null,"description":"Slab structure file (POSCAR/CONTCAR/CIF)."},"slab_dir":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string"},{"type":"null"}],"default":null,"description":"Directory containing slab files for high-throughput placement."},"adsorbate_file":{"description":"Adsorbate molecule file (XYZ).","type":"string"},"mode":{"default":"all","description":"all|ontop|bridge|hollow","type":"string"},"distance":{"default":2.0,"description":"Height used to generate adsorption sites (Å).","minimum":0.0,"type":"number"},"max_structures":{"default":1000,"description":"Maximum number of adsorbed structures to generate.","minimum":1,"type":"integer"},"output_dir":{"default":"adsorption/batch","description":"Directory to write batch POSCARs.","type":"string"}},"required":["adsorbate_file"],"type":"object","additionalProperties":false}}},{"type":"function","function":{"name":"make_neb_geometry","description":"Generate NEB interpolation geometries in nebmake.pl style.\n\n    The tool validates that initial and final structures have the same element order, atom count,\n    and lattice (within tolerance). Images are written under output_dir/00..(NI+1) with output_filename.\n    Selective dynamics constraints are preserved if present in the input files (ASE handles constraints).","parameters":{"properties":{"initial_path":{"description":"Initial structure file (POSCAR/CONTCAR/.vasp/.cif).","type":"string"},"final_path":{"description":"Final structure file (POSCAR/CONTCAR/.vasp/.cif).","type":"string"},"n_images":{"description":"Number of intermediate images (NI).","minimum":1,"type":"integer"},"output_dir":{"default":"neb_images","description":"Output directory for image folders (workspace-relative).","type":"string"},"output_filename":{"default":"POSCAR","description":"Filename for each image output (e.g., POSCAR).","type":"string"},"interp_mode":{"default":"direct","description":"Output coordinate style when writing POSCAR: direct (fractional) or cartesian.","pattern":"^(direct|cartesian)$","type":"string"},"interp_method":{"default":"linear","description":"Interpolation method: linear or idpp.","pattern":"^(linear|idpp)$","type":"string"},"vtst_wrap":{"default":true,"description":"If true, wrap fractional coordinates into [0,1) before interpolation (VTST nebmake.pl behavior).","type":"boolean"},"overwrite":{"default":false,"description":"If true, overwrite output_dir if it exists.","type":"boolean"}},"required":["initial_path","final_path","n_images"],"type":"object","additionalProperties":false}}},{"type":"function","function":{"name":"make_neb_incar","description":"Generate a VTST NEB/CI-NEB INCAR based on a template INCAR.\n\n    The tool parses the template INCAR (ignores comments/blank lines, case-insensitive keys),\n    applies NEB overrides, and writes the final INCAR along with a patch JSON.","parameters":{"properties":{"template_incar_path":{"description":"Template INCAR path (workspace-relative).","type":"string"},"output_incar_path":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string"},{"type":"null"}],"default":null,"description":"Output INCAR path. If omitted, uses output_dir/INCAR."},"output_dir":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string"},{"type":"null"}],"default":"neb_inputs","description":"Output directory for INCAR and patch JSON (workspace-relative)."},"images":{"description":"Number of intermediate images (IMAGES).","minimum":1,"type":"integer"},"climb":{"default":false,"description":"Enable CI-NEB with LCLIMB=.TRUE. if true.","type":"boolean"},"iopt":{"default":7,"description":"IOPT value for VTST optimizer (allowed: 7/2/1).","type":"integer"},"ediff":{"anyOf":[{"type":"number"},{"type":"null"}],"default":null,"description":"Override EDIFF if provided."},"ediffg":{"anyOf":[{"type":"number"},{"type":"null"}],"default":null,"description":"Override EDIFFG if provided."},"spring":{"anyOf":[{"type":"number"},{"type":"null"}],"default":null,"description":"Override SPRING if provided."},"potim":{"anyOf":[{"type":"number"},{"type":"null"}],"default":0.0,"description":"Override POTIM (default 0)."},"additional_overrides":{"additionalProperties":true,"description":"Additional INCAR overrides as a dict; highest priority and can override required defaults. In this tool, due to pymatgen constraints, MAGMOM/LDAUU/LDAUJ must be provided as symbol:value maps. If not provided, no user override is applied and this tool's default INCAR strategy is used. Use null value to remove a key from INCAR.","type":"object"}},"required":["template_incar_path","images"],"type":"object","additionalProperties":false}}},{"type":"function","function":{"name":"vasp_execute_batch","description":"Submit VASP runs in one DPDispatcher submission (single-folder or recursive batch modes).","parameters":{"properties":{"input_dir":{"description":"Input directory for VASP execution. Two modes are supported: (1) single-folder mode: input_dir itself is a VASP calc folder containing INCAR and POTCAR; (2) batch mode: recursively discover subfolders containing INCAR and POTCAR. Nested mode is forbidden when input_dir itself is a calc folder and descendants also contain calc folders.","type":"string"},"output_dir":{"description":"Root directory to store outputs. In single-folder mode, results go to output_dir/<basename(input_dir)>. In batch mode, results mirror discovered subfolder layout under output_dir. Must not be inside input_dir. Staging directories under output_dir are cleaned after completion.","type":"string"},"check_interval":{"default":30,"description":"Polling interval seconds","type":"integer"}},"required":["input_dir","output_dir"],"type":"object","additionalProperties":false}}},{"type":"function","function":{"name":"mp_search_materials","description":"Search Materials Project with flexible criteria and write results to CSV.\n\n    Common criteria keys (pass via `criteria`):\n      - material_ids (list[str] or str)\n      - elements (list[str] or str)\n      - chemsys (str)\n      - formula (str)\n      - is_stable (bool)\n      - energy_above_hull ([min, max])\n      - formation_energy ([min, max])\n      - band_gap ([min, max])\n      - crystal_system (str)\n      - spacegroup_number / spacegroup_symbol\n      - num_sites ([min, max])\n      - density ([min, max])\n      - volume ([min, max])\n      - num_elements ([min, max])\n    Common fields for output rows (pass via `fields`):\n      material_id, formula_pretty (or formula), energy_above_hull, formation_energy_per_atom (or formation_energy),\n      band_gap, crystal_system, spacegroup_number, spacegroup_symbol, nsites (or num_sites), density, volume.","parameters":{"properties":{"criteria":{"additionalProperties":true,"description":"Direct summary.search filters as a dict (keys listed above). Range values may be [min, max].","type":"object"},"fields":{"description":"Fields to include in CSV rows; supports common aliases.","items":{"type":"string"},"type":"array"},"limit":{"default":50,"description":"Maximum number of hits to return (default 50).","minimum":1,"type":"integer"},"output_csv":{"description":"Workspace-relative CSV path to write search results.","type":"string"}},"required":["output_csv"],"type":"object","additionalProperties":false}}},{"type":"function","function":{"name":"mp_download_structure","description":"Download one or more structures from Materials Project into the workspace.","parameters":{"properties":{"mp_ids":{"description":"Materials Project IDs, e.g., ['mp-149', 'mp-13'].","items":{"type":"string"},"type":"array"},"fmt":{"default":"poscar","description":"Output format: poscar|cif|json.","pattern":"^(poscar|cif|json)$","type":"string"},"output_dir":{"default":"retrieval/mp","description":"Workspace-relative directory to save the structure.","type":"string"}},"required":["mp_ids"],"type":"object","additionalProperties":false}}},{"type":"function","function":{"name":"bash_exec","description":"Execute a multi-line bash script inside the workspace (default) and return stdout/stderr.\n    Network access is disabled by default using Linux network namespaces (unshare).\n    Symbolic link operations are disabled; use copy/move operations instead.\n    Stdout/stderr are returned as-is and projection/offload is handled centrally.\n    Keep output short in scripts and print one-line summaries when possible.","parameters":{"properties":{"script":{"description":"Bash script to execute (multi-line).","type":"string"},"cwd":{"default":".","description":"Working directory inside project files root.","type":"string"},"timeout_s":{"default":86400.0,"description":"Timeout seconds.","minimum":0.1,"type":"number"},"no_network":{"default":true,"description":"Disable network using unshare network namespace.","type":"boolean"}},"required":["script"],"type":"object","additionalProperties":false}}},{"type":"function","function":{"name":"apply_aider_edits","description":"Apply Aider SEARCH/REPLACE edit blocks to workspace files.","parameters":{"properties":{"edits_text":{"description":"Aider SEARCH/REPLACE edit blocks text. Format per block:\n<relative/path/to/file>\n<<<<<<< SEARCH\n... exact existing text ...\n=======\n... replacement text ...\n>>>>>>> REPLACE","type":"string"},"allowed_paths":{"description":"Optional project-files-relative path prefixes. Use [] to allow edits anywhere under workspace root.","items":{"type":"string"},"type":"array"},"emit_diff":{"default":true,"description":"Whether to return unified diff text for audit.","type":"boolean"}},"required":["edits_text"],"type":"object","additionalProperties":false}}},{"type":"function","function":{"name":"read_text_file","description":"Read the complete contents of a file from the file system as text. Handles various text encodings and provides detailed error messages if the file cannot be read. Use this tool when you need to examine the contents of a single file. Use the 'head' parameter to read only the first N lines of a file, or the 'tail' parameter to read only the last N lines of a file. Operates on the file as text regardless of extension. Only works within allowed directories.","parameters":{"$schema":"http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#","type":"object","properties":{"path":{"type":"string"},"tail":{"description":"If provided, returns only the last N lines of the file","type":"number"},"head":{"description":"If provided, returns only the first N lines of the file","type":"number"}},"required":["path"]}}},{"type":"function","function":{"name":"read_multiple_files","description":"Read the contents of multiple files simultaneously. This is more efficient than reading files one by one when you need to analyze or compare multiple files. Each file's content is returned with its path as a reference. Failed reads for individual files won't stop the entire operation. Only works within allowed directories.","parameters":{"$schema":"http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#","type":"object","properties":{"paths":{"minItems":1,"type":"array","items":{"type":"string"},"description":"Array of file paths to read. Each path must be a string pointing to a valid file within allowed directories."}},"required":["paths"]}}},{"type":"function","function":{"name":"write_file","description":"Create a new file or completely overwrite an existing file with new content. Use with caution as it will overwrite existing files without warning. Handles text content with proper encoding. Only works within allowed directories.","parameters":{"$schema":"http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#","type":"object","properties":{"path":{"type":"string"},"content":{"type":"string"}},"required":["path","content"]}}},{"type":"function","function":{"name":"edit_file","description":"Make line-based edits to a text file. Each edit replaces exact line sequences with new content. Returns a git-style diff showing the changes made. Only works within allowed directories.","parameters":{"$schema":"http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#","type":"object","properties":{"path":{"type":"string"},"edits":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"object","properties":{"oldText":{"type":"string","description":"Text to search for - must match exactly"},"newText":{"type":"string","description":"Text to replace with"}},"required":["oldText","newText"]}},"dryRun":{"default":false,"description":"Preview changes using git-style diff format","type":"boolean"}},"required":["path","edits"]}}},{"type":"function","function":{"name":"create_directory","description":"Create a new directory or ensure a directory exists. Can create multiple nested directories in one operation. If the directory already exists, this operation will succeed silently. Perfect for setting up directory structures for projects or ensuring required paths exist. Only works within allowed directories.","parameters":{"$schema":"http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#","type":"object","properties":{"path":{"type":"string"}},"required":["path"]}}},{"type":"function","function":{"name":"list_directory","description":"Get a detailed listing of all files and directories in a specified path. Results clearly distinguish between files and directories with [FILE] and [DIR] prefixes. This tool is essential for understanding directory structure and finding specific files within a directory. Only works within allowed directories.","parameters":{"$schema":"http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#","type":"object","properties":{"path":{"type":"string"}},"required":["path"]}}},{"type":"function","function":{"name":"directory_tree","description":"Get a recursive tree view of files and directories as a JSON structure. Each entry includes 'name', 'type' (file/directory), and 'children' for directories. Files have no children array, while directories always have a children array (which may be empty). The output is formatted with 2-space indentation for readability. Only works within allowed directories.","parameters":{"$schema":"http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#","type":"object","properties":{"path":{"type":"string"},"excludePatterns":{"default":[],"type":"array","items":{"type":"string"}}},"required":["path"]}}},{"type":"function","function":{"name":"move_file","description":"Move or rename files and directories. Can move files between directories and rename them in a single operation. If the destination exists, the operation will fail. Works across different directories and can be used for simple renaming within the same directory. Both source and destination must be within allowed directories.","parameters":{"$schema":"http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#","type":"object","properties":{"source":{"type":"string"},"destination":{"type":"string"}},"required":["source","destination"]}}},{"type":"function","function":{"name":"search_files","description":"Recursively search for files and directories matching a pattern. The patterns should be glob-style patterns that match paths relative to the working directory. Use pattern like '*.ext' to match files in current directory, and '**/*.ext' to match files in all subdirectories. Returns full paths to all matching items. Great for finding files when you don't know their exact location. Only searches within allowed directories.","parameters":{"$schema":"http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#","type":"object","properties":{"path":{"type":"string"},"pattern":{"type":"string"},"excludePatterns":{"default":[],"type":"array","items":{"type":"string"}}},"required":["path","pattern"]}}},{"type":"function","function":{"name":"TaskOutput","description":"Structured output from the task runner agent.","parameters":{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"status":{"description":"Task terminal status. Use 'done' only when task acceptance criteria are satisfied; use 'blocked' when progress is blocked by unresolved issues.","enum":["done","blocked"],"type":"string"},"summary":{"description":"Concise task outcome/failure summary with key file pointers. Do not paste long tables/logs/scripts; cite file paths instead.","type":"string"},"facts":{"description":"Only high-value verified facts reusable downstream (include units/conditions/evidence path when relevant). Do not restate command traces. Use [] when none.","items":{"type":"string"},"type":"array"},"files":{"description":"Only key reproducibility/user-facing artifact paths (files or directories). Use a directory path when it is a clearer bundle-level reference. Avoid listing low-value scratch files. Use [] when none.","items":{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"path":{"description":"Workspace-relative artifact path (file or directory). Always use project-relative paths; do not use absolute paths.","type":"string"},"description":{"description":"Short one-line description.","type":"string"},"kind":{"description":"Artifact category. Common values: script, output, report, log. Use 'dir' when the path points to a directory bundle.","type":"string"}},"required":["path","description","kind"],"type":"object"},"type":"array"},"constraints":{"description":"Only new/changed constraints. Use [] when none.","items":{"type":"string"},"type":"array"},"open_questions":{"description":"Only unresolved blockers affecting next steps. Do not include speculative questions. Use [] when none.","items":{"type":"string"},"type":"array"},"decisions":{"description":"Only decisions materially affecting downstream work; avoid duplicating summary/facts content. Use [] when none.","items":{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"decision":{"description":"Short decision statement.","type":"string"},"rationale":{"description":"Brief rationale (one short sentence preferred).","type":"string"}},"required":["decision","rationale"],"type":"object"},"type":"array"},"next_steps":{"description":"Only immediate actionable next steps. Use [] when no next step is required.","items":{"type":"string"},"type":"array"},"artifacts":{"description":"Supporting artifact paths when needed. Use [] when none.","items":{"type":"string"},"type":"array"},"error":{"description":"Failure reason for status=blocked. For status=done, use empty string ''.","type":"string"},"needs_human":{"description":"Whether a human must intervene for status=blocked. For status=done, set false.","type":"boolean"},"hint":{"description":"Optional concise recovery hint for status=blocked. For status=done, use empty string ''.","type":"string"}},"required":["status","summary","facts","files","constraints","open_questions","decisions","next_steps","artifacts","error","needs_human","hint"],"type":"object"}}}],"prompt_cache_retention":"24h"}
17:22:41 INFO httpx | HTTP Request: POST https://openrouter.ai/api/v1/chat/completions "HTTP/1.1 200 OK"
17:22:55 INFO catmaster.llm.factory | [llm.http.raw_post] provider=openrouter model=openai/gpt-5.3-codex:online method=POST url=https://openrouter.ai/api/v1/chat/completions body={"messages":[{"content":"You are an execution controller. Use tool calling to advance the current task.\n\nPriority rules:\n- Use tool calling from all available tools to achieve the goal in the context pack.\n- Check tool names and params carefully.\n- Treat memory index as cross-run historical memory from prior decisions/scientific invariant updates and it may lag current-run progress.\n- For current execution, task packet (goal/detail/expected outputs) is authoritative; use memory for reusable invariants and prior-run context only.\n- Task detail defines the task invariants and done checks. Execute with the minimal non-destructive procedure that satisfies those invariants. Treat task-detail parameters as preferred unless explicitly marked hard, and do bounded self-adjustments before escalating while keeping scientific/computational invariants fixed.\n- Tool schemas are authoritative for argument shapes/defaults; do not re-invent parameter templates in bash scripts.\n- Do not initiate file edits on your own. Only edit files when the current task packet explicitly requires editing/writing outputs for this task. For `MEMORY/**`, only update when scientific invariants, method definitions, or final reusable results changed.\n- If file editing is explicitly required by the task packet, prefer `apply_aider_edits` for deterministic edits (including memory files) over ad-hoc in-place shell edits.\n\nExecution rules:\n- Do not rerun the same preparation tool with identical parameters if the previous call already succeeded and required artifacts still exist. Prefer reusing and validating existing outputs.\n- Do not trigger expensive reruns purely for path/layout normalization when numerical/physical requirements are already satisfied.\n- Bundle independent filesystem operations in the same turn whenever possible, but do not issue concurrent write calls; keep write/edit/move/create operations sequential and verify each write step before the next.\n- For simple multi-directory setup or one-shot workspace reconnaissance, prefer a single focused bash_exec over many single-path filesystem tool calls.\n- Perform only checks required to satisfy current done criteria; avoid speculative or perfection-oriented extra validation.\n- For routine checks, keep bash output small: prefer focused queries (`rg -n`, `head`, `tail`) and avoid broad/full-file dumps unless deep debugging is required.\n- Prefer read_multiple_files when you need several small text files at once.\n- Progressive disclosure is mandatory: memory_index_excerpt is short; discover paths with `search_files` / `list_directory` / `directory_tree`, then read small windows via `read_text_file(head=..., tail=...)`.\n- Use `bash_exec` for shell execution, content grep (`rg`), parser invocation, and external binaries.\n- Internal metadata audit logs are not task inputs; do not read or reference them in task reasoning.\n- By default, do not generate long markdown reports via `cat <<'MD'`.\n\nParsing policy:\n- Debug triage should prioritize focused, minimal evidence extraction and concise failure signatures.\n- For extracting final numerical results across many calculations (for comparison/reporting), avoid repeated manual grep stitching; prefer parser libraries or small single-purpose scripts.\n- Prefer mature third-party libraries for parsing and post-analysis when available; avoid reimplementing standard parsers/analysis logic from scratch.\n- Common Python packages are available and preferred when relevant: ase, pymatgen, numpy, matplotlib, scipy, pandas, fitz, requests.\n- For actual workload execution (batch processing, long runs, or outputs to be reused/audited), write reusable script files and keep each script focused/small.\n\nTermination and handoff:\n- End with one concise final handoff that clearly states the task status and reusable outputs.\n- Use `status=\"done\"` when task is complete.\n- Use `status=\"blocked\"` only when still blocked after bounded self-adjustment attempts on non-critical execution parameters, or when hard scientific invariants conflict.\n- Follow schema field descriptions for per-field content quality and placeholders; do not fill fields with invented content.\n- For remote/batch job failures, do one minimal triage (failing status file, stdout/stderr snippets, key inputs) and attempt one focused fix.\n- Do not do open-ended exploration for remote failures (no SSH). If failure persists, return `status=\"blocked\"` with failed paths, evidence pointers, likely cause, and a minimal rerun/repair plan that reruns only the failed subset.\n- Keep handoff evidence-based and concise; avoid redundant repetition across fields.\n- Function tools must be invoked via tool calls. Do NOT put function tool names into bash_exec commands.\n- Keep stdout concise; if persistent command logs are needed, use pipeline logging to project files (e.g., `cmd 2>&1 | tee reports/<task_desc>/run.log`) and print short summaries.\n- Always provide file or directory paths as relative paths; they will be resolved relative to the project files root.\n","role":"system"},{"content":"<context_pack>\nTask goal:\nRun a VASP relaxation for gas-phase O2 in a large cubic box and extract final energy/atom and O–O bond length.\n\nTask detail:\n1) Create a new workdir `o2_vasp/relax/`.\n2) Build O2 geometry (SMILES `O=O`) and place in a cubic cell with ~15–20 Å vacuum (e.g., 18 Å) centered; write a structure file usable by VASP prep (POSCAR or an intermediate format your prep tool accepts).\n3) Prepare VASP relaxation inputs from scratch in that folder (INCAR/KPOINTS/POSCAR/POTCAR) using PBE PAW for O. Use Gamma-only KPOINTS 1x1x1. Use spin-polarization for triplet O2 (ISPIN=2; initialize MAGMOM ~1 1 and/or set NUPDOWN=2). Recommend: PREC=Accurate, ENCUT=520 (or >= POTCAR ENMAX), EDIFF=1e-6, EDIFFG=-0.02, ISMEAR=0 SIGMA=0.05, IBRION=2, NSW=100, ISIF=2, ISYM=0, LCHARG=.FALSE., LWAVE=.FALSE.\n4) Execute VASP in that directory (single job) until convergence. Ensure outputs include OUTCAR, OSZICAR, CONTCAR.\n5) Parse results: (a) final TOTEN from OUTCAR (last ionic step) and compute energy per atom = TOTEN/2 in eV/atom; (b) compute O–O distance from CONTCAR final positions (Å).\n6) Write a short `o2_vasp/RESULTS.md` summarizing: settings used, final energy (eV), energy/atom (eV/atom), bond length (Å), and point to evidence lines/paths (e.g., OUTCAR grep output, CONTCAR).\n\nExpected outputs:\n- Directory `o2_vasp/relax/` containing INCAR, KPOINTS, POSCAR, POTCAR, and VASP outputs (OUTCAR, OSZICAR, CONTCAR).\n- `o2_vasp/RESULTS.md` with final TOTEN (eV), energy per atom (eV/atom), and O–O bond length (Å) plus file/line references or extracted snippets.\n\nSuggested tools:\ncreate_molecule_from_smiles, vasp_relax_prepare, vasp_execute_batch, bash_exec, read_text_file, write_file\n\nReference hint:\n- If `vasp_relax_prepare` needs a structure file, generate an XYZ first then convert/write POSCAR.\n- Use `grep -n \"free  energy   TOTEN\" OUTCAR | tail -1` to capture final TOTEN line.\n- Bond length: parse CONTCAR (Cartesian) and compute distance between the two atoms via a tiny python snippet in bash.\n\nWorkspace policy:\nProject files policy:\n- Treat \".\" as the project files root.\n- All path parameters and returned paths are relative to \".\".\n- Never use absolute paths or metadata paths.\n- Use search_files / list_directory / directory_tree to discover files.\n- Use read_text_file with head/tail for progressive disclosure.\n- Use bash_exec for shell commands, content grep, parser invocation, and external binaries.\n- Role: task_runner\n\nMemory index excerpt:\n# MEMORY (AUTOLOADED INDEX)\n\n## What this is\n- Autoloaded memory index for this project.\n- Keep this file concise and pointer-first.\n- Put details in MEMORY/topics/*.md.\n\n## Latest State\n- Current focus: Compute O2 in a box: prepare VASP inputs from scratch, DO perform VASP calculation to get the results, and report final energy per atom and O–O bond distance from vasp results.\n- Current milestone: (empty)\n- Latest run artifact: (empty)\n- Next action: (empty)\n\n## Top Constraints\n1. (empty)\n\n## Active Open Questions\n1. (empty)\n\n## Pointers\n- Facts / decisions: MEMORY/topics/FACTS.md\n- Files / artifacts: MEMORY/topics/FILES.md\n- Constraints: MEMORY/topics/CONSTRAINTS.md\n- Open questions: MEMORY/topics/QUESTIONS.md\n- Runbook: MEMORY/topics/RUNBOOK.md\n\n## Keyword Map\n- GOAL: objective, success criteria, scope, non-goals\n- FACTS: definition, verified, result, decision\n- FILES: path, artifact, dataset, output, script\n- CONSTRAINTS: must, cannot, policy, budget\n- QUESTIONS: unknown, blocked, clarify, decide\n- RUNBOOK: steps, checklist, verify\n\n</context_pack>\n","role":"user"},{"content":null,"role":"assistant","tool_calls":[{"type":"function","id":"call_NLAqyx4HYI4uImLrpUJQ3jgo","function":{"name":"bash_exec","arguments":"{\"script\": \"set -e\\nmkdir -p o2_vasp/relax\\nprintf 'created o2_vasp/relax\\\\n'\\nls -la o2_vasp\", \"cwd\": \".\", \"timeout_s\": 120, \"no_network\": true}"}}]},{"content":"stdout:\ncreated o2_vasp/relax\ntotal 12\ndrwxr-xr-x 3 root root 4096 Mar  3 17:21 .\ndrwxr-xr-x 4 root root 4096 Mar  3 17:21 ..\ndrwxr-xr-x 2 root root 4096 Mar  3 17:21 relax\n\nexit_code=0 timed_out=False cancelled=False cwd=. timeout_s=120.0\nOffload: _tool_outputs/bash_exec/bash_exec_20260303T092152947189Z_bf00889a.json","role":"tool","tool_call_id":"call_NLAqyx4HYI4uImLrpUJQ3jgo"},{"content":null,"role":"assistant","tool_calls":[{"type":"function","id":"call_4wr72H1u1SwOyVJwdFqACxhS","function":{"name":"create_molecule_from_smiles","arguments":"{\"smiles\": \"O=O\", \"name\": \"O2\", \"output_path\": \"o2_vasp/relax/o2\", \"box_padding\": 9, \"fmt\": \"both\"}"}}]},{"content":"create_molecule_from_smiles completed.\nformula=O